\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-China's spot yuan drops below guidance rate for first time since 2012\b0\par\par\uc2 1,054 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2014\par 06:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Adds comments, background)\par     * Yuan falls below midpoint for first time since Sept, 2012\par     * Yuan to remain subdued in near term - traders\par     * Upward trend for the yuan expected to remain intact this\par year\par     * Daily trading band expected to widen soon\par \par     By Michelle Chen and Pete Sweeney\par     HONG KONG, Feb 25 (Reuters) - China's spot yuan fell below\par the official midpoint rate for the first time since September\par 2012 on Tuesday, as economists and traders suspected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to add volatility to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par preparation for reform.\par     Spot yuan has entered a dramatic weakening cycle\par in recent weeks, guided downward by a series of weak fixings by\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with additional momentum added to the slide by\par the unwinding of yuan positions by Chinese banks.   \par     The exchange rate is allowed to move 1 percent above or\par below the midpoint setting on any given day, a range referred to\par as the daily trading band. Traders believe the recent\par depreciation is intended to set the stage for widening that band\par to 2 percent or more.\par    The yuan touched 6.1250 per dollar on Tuesday morning, much\par softer than the midpoint which was set at 6.1184.\par     In addition to using the midpoint to drive the market down,\par traders said that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 was\par discreetly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot market.\par     "It's quite obvious that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is buying dollars\par in the market via state-owned banks, trying to create\par depreciation expectations for the yuan," said a trader at a\par Chinese bank based in Shanghai.\par     Regardless, the result has been the realignment of the spot\par price with the midpoint setting. Previously the spot market\par consistently priced the yuan near the strongest permissible\par rate, suggesting companies and other market participants were\par betting on further appreciation.\par     By Tuesday, the spread had narrowed such that the spot price\par was only 0.16 percent away from the midpoint. The yuan's\par exchange rate in offshore markets has fallen more than\par one percent in the past week and was even weaker than its\par onshore counterpart at some point last week.\par     Andy Ji, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of\par Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore, said the spread between the onshore yuan\par and the offshore version had narrowed significantly, suggesting\par offshore investors were also finally unwinding long yuan\par positions. \par     Ji said a sustained depreciation would risk pouring more\par yuan into the domestic money supply, aggravating credit\par expansion, but that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was trying to realign\par onshore and offshore markets after a period of passivity.  \par    "(The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) wanted to get back to the driver's seat\par and it did."\par     The abruptness of the change has been mildly startling\par nevertheless, and there are disagreements over its significance\par given the strong bullishness toward yuan assets from foreign and\par domestic investors.\par     The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been a favorite among emerging\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2013, gaining nearly 3 percent even as most\par of its peers depreciated against the dollar. Most analysts\par expect it to appreciate another 2-3 percent this year, but the\par change in direction has rattled confidence.\par     Economists say that may be the policy objective. Beijing\par wants to introduce more bi-directional volatility into the\par market to indirectly challenge the common assumption that the\par yuan is a one-way bet.\par     That assumption is blamed for repeated distorted readings on\par China's trade, warped by manipulated invoices trying to sneak\par more capital into the country.\par     Theoretically, widening the trading band would give the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more room to rise and fall, and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par been suggesting widening has been imminent since April 2013.\par     Analysts think the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  may act before the upcoming National\par People's Congress meeting set to open March 5, although other\par potential triggers could include U.S. President Barack Obama's\par visit to Asia, or the publication of a \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  foreign\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy report in April.     \par     Despite the recent change of direction, analysts believe the\par upward trend of the "redback" remains intact given China's\par strong trade surplus and continued capital inflows, not to\par mention the Chinese government's desire to promote its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to global investors.\par     "We believe introducing two-way volatility is consistent\par with \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's medium-term objective to increase the flexibility of\par RMB exchange rate and move RMB towards convertibility, and does\par not suggest \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is shifting exchange rate policy bias towards\par actively weakening the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," wrote Linan Liu and Perry\par Kojodjojo of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a research note.         \par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par     \par  Item                        Current    Previous    Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.1184     6.1189      0.01%\par  Spot yuan                   6.1086     6.0984      -0.17%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   -0.16%                 \par  Spot change ytd                                    1.99%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 35.49%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 1 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par     \par  Instrument                 Current   Difference from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan         6.1065    0.04%\par                                       \par  Offshore non-deliverable   6.14      -0.35%\par  forwards                             \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par      - New quotas rekindle debate over dim sum market's future\par  \par      - Flood of offshore yuan bonds may spark higher yields\par  \par     - China investors face bumpy ride as reform speculation\par intensifies \par     - CHINA MONEY - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  preparing market for more yuan\par volatility \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan is positive outlier compared with plunging emerging\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Hot money tracker: Hot money inflows slowed to a trickle\par in December 2013 GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/saz74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/saz74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Corporate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  behavior reflects yuan appreciation\par expectations. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange rate, the\par yuan is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par    >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par \par  (Additional reporting by Jongwoo Cheon in Singapore; Editing by\par Vidya Ranganathan and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jacqueline Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2 )\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-2-28T05:28:55.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140225ea2p005et\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
