\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  Yuan Down on \uc2 PBOC \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2014\par 11:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                   Vs Parity  Previous \par USD/CNY Central Parity   6.1070               6.1100 \par USD/CNY OTC 0830 GMT     6.0668    -0.66%     6.0636 \par             High         6.0672    -0.65% \par             Low          6.0613    -0.75% \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI--China's yuan fell against the U.S. dollar late Friday as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  purchased the dollar through big banks, according to traders, despite guiding the yuan fixing higher on the dollar's overseas weakness.\f28 \par \par \uc2 On the over-the-counter market, the dollar was at CNY6.0668 around 0830 GMT, higher than Thursday's close of CNY6.0636. It traded in a range of CNY6.0613 to CNY6.0672.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  set the dollar/yuan central parity rate at 6.1070, lower than Thursday's 6.1100, after the dollar dropped against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the release of disappointing data on retail sales and jobless claims.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-yuan pair fell in the morning, taking the lead from the central parity. But the pair turned higher in the afternoon on suspected dollar buying supported by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said traders.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  is guiding the yuan weaker or slowing its rising pace. There was massive dollar selling from banking customers since January. Maybe the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  is trying to curb this trend," said a Shanghai-based local bank trader.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has fallen 0.2% since the start of this year after gaining 2.9% in 2013.\par \par \uc2 Offshore, one-year dollar/yuan nondeliverable forward contracts fell to 6.1081/6.1118 from 6.1105/6.1142 late Thursday, implying a 0.7% fall by the yuan over the next year.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore yuan market in Hong Kong, where the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  floats freely, the dollar was at CNY6.0373, lower than CNY6.0419 late Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Wynne Wang at wynne.wang@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 14-02-14 1020GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020140214ea2e0007f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
