\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan touches another record high after midpoint guidance\b0\par\par\uc2 606 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2014\par 07:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yuan at record high for 2nd straight day\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  sets an all-time high midpoint\par     * Traders suspect \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues\par     By Michelle Chen\par     HONG KONG, Jan 14 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan touched a record\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 high for a second day on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again set a stronger official midpoint, which prompted investors to increase their long bets on the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The yuan opened at an all-time high of 6.0415 per dollar and reached 6.0414 near midday, up 0.03 percent from Monday's close of 6.0434. \uc2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 guided its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into strong territory again by fixing the midpoint at 6.0930, up 0.03 percent from the previous day's 6.0950, in response to an overnight fall in the dollar index. "We see strong demand to sell dollars from clients, and if it were not the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  who \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, the spot would have risen much faster," said a trader at a Chinese bank in Shanghai. Last year, the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  was suspected to have stepped in from time to time via big Chinese banks to keep the yuan from strengthening too much. Traders said they haven't seen changes to that mechanism so far this year. The yuan has risen 0.2 percent against the dollar this year. In 2013, it gained 2.9 percent, outperforming all other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has appreciated 37 percent since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2005 revaluation. Traders believe the appreciation trend of the "redback" is intact as Beijing accelerates reform of its financial markets, though the pace at which the U.S. Federal Reserve tapers its monetary stimulus remains an uncertainty. "If the Fed scales back faster than expected later this year, it may affect the dollar movement as well as the yuan," the trader in Shanghai said.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:      \par  Item                        Current   Previous   Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.093     6.095      0.03%\par  Spot yuan                   6.0414    6.0434     0.03%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   -0.85%               \par  Spot change ytd                                  3.13%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation               37.00%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to rise or fall 1 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each morning. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par         \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par     \par  Instrument                 Current   Difference from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan         6.0234    0.30%*\par                                       \par  Offshore non-deliverable   6.0993    -0.10%**\par  forwards                             \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Premium for offshore spot over onshore **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint, since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint. . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - Hot money distorts China's exports as speculators seek to\par cash in on yuan, rate reforms\par     - China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suggests faster tempo for freeing yuan\par  \par     - China investors face bumpy ride as reform speculation\par intensifies \par     - CHINA MONEY - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  preparing market for more yuan\par volatility \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Hot money returned to China in Sept, Oct after two months\par of outflows GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/saz74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/saz74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Corporate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  behavior reflects yuan appreciation\par expectations. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange rate, the\par yuan is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par    >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Richard Borsuk)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-MIDDAY/ | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140117ea1e0007a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
