\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-POLL-China yuan set for modest gain in 2014 as Fed tapering looms\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2014\par 08:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Refiles to fix RIC for yuan in paragraph 2)\par \par \uc2 BEIJING, Jan 9 (Reuters) - China's yuan is likely to gain 1.7 percent versus the dollar in 2014 due to capital inflows, even as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  draws some support from the Federal Reserve's move to unwind its economic stimulus, according to a Reuters poll.\par \par \uc2 The median forecasts in a poll of 26 analysts showed the yuan may creep up to 6.05 against the dollar in three months, and to 6.00 in six months and 5.95 in 12 months. That compares with Wednesday's close of 6.0512..\par \par \uc2 The yuan has gained nearly 37 percent against the dollar since its landmark revaluation in 2005, including a 2.9 percent rise in 2013. Many traders see a similar 3 percent gain this year.\par \par \uc2 "The pace of yuan appreciation may slow in 2014, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's two-way volatility may increase," said Nie Wen, an economist at Hwabao Trust in Shanghai.\par \par \uc2 The Fed has decided to cut its asset-purchase program, known as quantitative easing, or QE, by $10 billion to $75 billion per month, which may lend further support to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Short-term capital inflows have been the key driver of recent yuan appreciation, but further strengthening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to be limited," said Minggao Shen, China economist at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 A speculative carry trade has been supporting the yuan in recent weeks as investors borrow cheaper offshore funds and channel money into China for higher yields, analysts say.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to temper the yuan's rise, especially as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  approaches the psychologically important 6 level, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pledged to reduce its regular \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make the yuan more flexible, but analysts doubt that will happen soon given fears of volatile fund flows as the Fed unwinds its stimulus.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Yao and Li Ran; Editing by Kim Coghill)\par \par \uc2 CHINA-YUAN/ (POLL,CORRECTED) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140112ea190002m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
