\par\par \b \uc2 China Shares End Higher on Reforms Hopes; Media, Defense Stocks Jump\b0\par\par\uc2 767 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2013\par 09:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI--China's shares ended higher on growing risk appetite, after the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief assured investors that China is moving ahead with financial-reform plans including liberalization of deposit rates and a more flexible yuan regime.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Shanghai Composite Index, which tracks both A and B shares, ended up 0.8% at 2201.07. Trading volume for the Shanghai index rose to CNY102.2 billion ($16.8 billion) from Tuesday's CNY84.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 The Shenzhen Composite Index rose 1.4% to 1069.26.\par \par \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  Governor \uc2 Zhou Xiaochuan\uc2  said Tuesday that Beijing plans to relax domestic interest-rate rules and reduce its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the state-run \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Securities Journal's website reported.\par \par \uc2 In a speech at a financial forum, Mr. Zhou also called for expanded quotas under the qualified domestic institutional investors and qualified foreign institutional investors programs, which cover inbound and outbound investments by institutions.\par \par \uc2 "These remarks show that China's moving towards its goal of making the economy more market oriented. Apparently they are welcomed by investors," \uc2 Everbright Securities\uc2  analyst Zeng Xianzhao said.\par \par \uc2 The economic reform blueprint published by policymakers two weeks ago "raises investor appetite for risks over the medium- to long-term," Shenyin Wanguo Securities analyst Wang Sheng said.\par \par \uc2 Still, Mr. Zeng cautioned against chasing the rally because stock market liquidity conditions tend to be tighter during the year-end.\par \par \uc2 Media and defense stocks were among biggest gainers Wednesday as investors bet on these stocks seen as beneficiaries of potential supportive measures by Beijing.\par \par \uc2 Huayi Brothers Media\uc2  hit its 10% daily upside limit at CNY30.32, \uc2 People.cn Co\uc2 . jumped 5.6% to CNY78.41, while China Aerospace Times Electronics gained 8.8% to CNY10.46.\par \par \uc2 Securities companies strengthened on expectations that market reforms would ease restrictions on the sector and bring in higher revenue, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Sinolink Securities\uc2  rose by its 10% daily upside limit at CNY17.69, Haitong Securities added 3.4% to CNY11.73 and \uc2 Citic Securities\uc2  advanced 3.1% to CNY12.91.\par \par \uc2 The December index futures contract, the most actively traded of the four index futures contracts traded in China, ended up 1.2% at 2422.4.\par \par \uc2 The futures are referenced to the CSI-300, an index of 300 Shanghai- and Shenzhen-listed yuan-denominated A shares. The CSI-300 ended 1.1% higher at 2414.48.\par \par \uc2 Write to Amy Li at amy.li@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 28 Nov 2013 02:33 EDT  China Shares Rise, Helped by Expectations for Coal Sector Reforms\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI--China's shares finished higher Thursday with a boost from gains in the coal sector.\par \par \uc2 The Shanghai Composite Index gained 0.8% to 2219.4. The Shenzhen index was last up 1.0% to 1079.9.\par \par \uc2 The gains came after China's State Council said in a draft proposal Thursday posted on the central government's website that China plans to accelerate the reform of its coal industry, shutting smaller mines to consolidate domestic production and experimenting with tariff levels to encourage higher-quality imports. Citing falling coal prices and industry losses, China's equivalent to a cabinet said it aimed to "curb the disorderly growth of coal production."\par \par \uc2 "Coals stocks have been soaring in recent weeks in part because storage of coal rises in anticipation of the snowy winter months in northern China," says Zeng Xianzhao, securities analyst with Everbright. "Valuations have also been improving because investors are anticipating high coal prices amid a likely move by the government to further limit the industry's total production levels," he adds.\par \par \uc2 Yanzhou Coal Mining Co\uc2 . was up 3.0% to CNY10.42, while Jiangxi Copper was up 4.7% to CNY15.46.\par \par \uc2 Stocks in other heavy industries also rose. \uc2 Rising Nonferrous Metals Share Co\uc2 . jumped the 10% daily limit to CNY45.08 and \uc2 Inner Mongolia Baotou Steel Rare-Earth (Group) Hi-Tech\uc2  Co. (600111.SH) advanced 8.4% to CNY27.27. \uc2 China Shenhua Energy Co. Ltd\uc2 . was up 1.6% at CNY17.06.\par \par \uc2 The Shanghai Composite remains down by 2.2% for the year to date, despite the market's recent rally on expectations for various reforms from Beijing. With around a month left to the year, Gerry Alfonso, strategist with Shenyin Wanguo Securities, says the mainland stock market will likely finish roughly flat or slightly negative, given that traders usually cash in some profits toward year-end.\par \par \uc2 Write to Chao Deng at chao.deng@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 28, 2013 02:33 ET (07:33 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131127e9br000pp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
