\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 3-China  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  suggests faster tempo for freeing yuan\b0\par\par\uc2 By Aileen Wang and Kevin Yao   \par \uc2 1,186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2013\par 07:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BEIJING, Nov 20 (Reuters) - With a shift in tone and language, \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor has dangled the prospect of speeding up \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform and giving markets more room to set the yuan's exchange rate as he underlines broader plans for sweeping economic change.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  under \uc2 Zhou Xiaochuan\uc2  has consistently flagged its intention to liberalise financial markets and allow the yuan to trade more freely, even before the Communist Party's top brass unveiled late last week the boldest set of economic and social reforms in nearly three decades.\par \par \uc2 But since the 60-point reform plan was released, Zhou has suggested urgency in pushing for change, although he has not provided any specific timetable. He promised on Saturday to "pull out all stops to deepen financial sector reforms".\par \par \uc2 Dariusz Kowalczyk, an economist at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  in Hong Kong, said the governor's comments could mean that the \uc2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 will widen the trading band of the yuan in the near term.\par \par \uc2 "That probably means there is more upside for the renminbi," he said. The yuan, also known as the renminbi, has risen this year to 6.09 per dollar from 6.23 at the end of 2012 and hit a record high of close to 6.08 in October.\par \par \uc2 However, there was little evidence of any new found freedom for the yuan in trading on Wednesday. On the one hand, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its daily fixing for the starting point of yuan trade at a record high, but dealers said open market gains were checked by state-run banks selling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , probably on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In addition, the daily fixing has been consistently weaker than the spot market, indicating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to rein in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  is still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to prevent the CNY (yuan) from appreciating more," said RBS economists Louis Kuijs and Tiffany Qiu in a client note, referring to dollar trade inflows and speculation that are putting the yuan under pressure to rise.\par \par \uc2 "Freeing up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would imply a very large appreciation versus the USD (dollar), something for which we believe there would not be appetite right now."\par \par \uc2 "BASICALLY"\par \par \uc2 Zhou's latest comments were released as part of a public guide book to the Communist Party's reforms, on sale in bookshops for 30 yuan ($5).\par \par \uc2 At more than 300 pages, it provides the full text of the Communist Party's blueprint and an explanation of the changes by President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 . It includes articles by top officials, such as Zhou.\par \par \uc2 In the guide book, Zhou says the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would gradually expand the yuan's trading band to help make the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more flexible and market-driven - comments that repeat a long-standing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  position.\par \par \uc2 "We will widen the floating range of the yuan exchange rate in an orderly manner and increase the two-way flexibility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Zhou was quoted as saying.\par \par \uc2 To that end, the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  will "basically" exit from regular \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, he said, going slightly further than in previous comments when he had said it would reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For years, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought up \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , mostly dollars, to curb strength in the yuan fuelled by the country's export engine, building the world's biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stockpile of $3.66 trillion.\par \par \uc2 Such \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a key driver of money and credit expansion, fanning inflationary risks and housing bubbles.\par \par \uc2 The yuan's trading band was last widened in April 2012 to allow the exchange rate to rise or fall 1 percent either side of the midpoint fixing announced daily by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We must seize the favorable time window to quicken the pace of realising yuan convertibility in capital account," Zhou said.\par \par \uc2 Full convertibility would allow the free movement of capital across China's borders, a demand of many of China's trading partners. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pledged to make the yuan "basically convertible" by 2015, but it has not made clear what that means.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts caution against high expectations for the speed of financial reform, noting some policymakers fear allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move freely too quickly could expose the economy to volatile capital flows, such as the ones blamed on the U.S. Federal Reserve's economic stimulus programme.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to unveil a long-awaited deposit insurance system by the end of this year or early in 2014 to pave the way for freeing up bank deposit rates, which are now subject to administrative caps.\par \par \uc2 Such a scheme would protect depositors as Beijing is concerned some smaller lenders could go under as banks compete for deposits in a more open regime. Earlier this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  removed controls on lending rates.\par \par \uc2 "We will choose a time when conditions are ripe to life controls on deposit rates, which we think is the final step of liberalising interest rates," \uc2 PBOC\uc2  Vice Governor Hu Xiaolian told a forum in Beijing on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "FAVORABLE WINDOW"\par \par \uc2 The reforms are aimed at helping Beijing engineer a shift in the giant economy away from investment- and exports-led growth to activity fuelled more by consumption and services.\par \par \uc2 The OECD, in forecasting China's economic growth would pick up to 8.2 percent in 2014 from 7.7 percent this year, urged Beijing to quicken its reforms while growth is holding steady.\par \par \uc2 "There is now a favorable window," the \uc2 Organisation for Economic Co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Development\uc2  said in an update of its global forecasts.\par \par \uc2 While the Communist Party leaders set the direction for reform in a four-day conclave that ended last week, it will be up to government ministries and agencies to put them into effect.\par \par \uc2 The head of the country's top economic planning agency promised fast results in an interview with the People's Daily, the Communist Party's official newspaper.\par \par \uc2 "We should quickly launch a batch of projects in financial, oil, power, railway, telecommunications, resource exploration, public utilities to attract private-sector investment," Xu Shaoshi, chairman of the \uc2 National Development and Reform Commission\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Another senior official, Yang Weimin, vice head of the Office of the Central Leading Group on Finance and Economic Affairs, told a news briefing that reforms would help ease local government debt, although he didn't explain how.\par \par \uc2 An explosion in local government debt accompanied Beijing's response to the global financial crisis and many analysts see it as a major risk hanging over the economy.\par \par \uc2 Yang said the reforms would include more tax revenues for local governments, allowing qualified localities to sell bonds, and setting up a new policy bank to fund urban infrastructure and housing projects under Beijing's urbanisation drive.\par \par \uc2 CHINA-REFORM/ (WRAPUP 3) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | G | RBN | J | ABX | BNX | FUN | AFA | CSA | LBY | RWSA | RWS | REULB | GNS | Z | RNP | DNP | PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131120e9bk0009z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
