\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan steadies on suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  by \uc2 PBOC\b0\par\par\uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2013\par 05:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 By Michelle Chen HONG KONG, Nov 15 (Reuters) - China's yuan steadied against the dollar on Friday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  via big state-owned banks to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise after an early bout of dollar-selling by companies. Traders expect the yuan to stay in a tight range and 6.09 remains a psychological barrier in the near term until the \uc2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 gives a clear signal to allow a fresh round of appreciation. Spot yuan traded at 6.0912 per dollar near midday, up 0.02 percent from Thursday's close of 6.0922. The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  fixed the yuan's midpoint at 6.1351, 0.06 percent weaker than the previous day's 6.1315. "There was strong dollar selling after the opening, which pushed the yuan to 6.0911, but then big state-owned banks came in to buy dollars immediately," said a trader at a Chinese bank in Shanghai.\par \par \uc2  "We thought the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would let the yuan appreciate more toward the year-end, but sustaining \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  made us curious where it would like it to move," the trader said. The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen more than 2 percent so far this year and its steady rise has attracted capital flows from global investors who have sought shelter from other volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Capital inflows to the "redback" may be further supported given that the U.S. is likely to continue its ultra-easy monetary policy until a durable economic recovery is in place that can sustain job creation. Fed Vice Chair \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  on Thursday robustly defended the Federal Reserve's bold steps to spur economic growth, calling efforts to boost hiring an "imperative" at a hearing into her nomination to become the first woman to lead the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Market participants are also waiting for more details of China's reform plans, which are usually announced a week after the conclusion of the Communist Party's third plenum on Tuesday. The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    \par  Item                        Current    Previous   Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.1351     6.1315     -0.06%\par  Spot yuan                   6.0912     6.0922     0.02%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   -0.72%                \par  Spot change ytd                                   2.28%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                35.88%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to rise or fall 1 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each morning. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET    \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par     \par  Instrument                 Current   Difference from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan         6.0779    0.22%*\par                                       \par  Offshore non-deliverable   6.163     -0.45%**\par  forwards                             \par     \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Premium for offshore spot over onshore **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint, since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint. . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par       - Gap between \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint and spot rate is narrowing.\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qyx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qyx74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Corporate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  purchases in May show reduction in yuan\par appreciation expectations. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Hot money inflows turn to outflows in May GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/saz74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/saz74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange rate, the\par yuan is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par       >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chris Gallagher\f28 \uc2 \f2 )\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN/MIDDAY | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131118e9bf00049\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
