\par\par \b \uc2 China's c.bank keeps spot yuan flat, midpoint near record high\b0\par\par\uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2013\par 06:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 PBOC\uc2  sets strong fix but seen curbing gains in market\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Seen preventing yuan from firming far beyond 6.12/dlr\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's will to keep yuan stable may be tested end-Sept\par     By Lu Jianxin and Pete Sweeney\par     SHANGHAI, Sept 11 (Reuters) - China's yuan was little\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 changed against the dollar on Wednesday as dealers attributed the spot market's stability to possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \uc2 The People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  (PBOC) \uc2 set a firmer midpoint before the market open, pegging it only three pips away from its record high, but traders suspected the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  had also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through major banks to restrain gains. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to want to narrow the gap between its official midpoint and the spot exchange rate, which has mostly remained near its upper limit of 1 percent stronger than the midpoint since late last year, buoyed by a general oversupply of dollars in the domestic market, traders said. Economists say that if Beijing can get the midpoint and the spot rate in closer alignment, it can then widen the intra-day trading band that currently holds the traded exchange rate within 1 percent of the midpoint in either direction. Spot yuan changed hands at 6.1197 per dollar at midday, almost unchanged from Tuesday's close of 6.1200. Before trading began, the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  set its midpoint at 6.1601, or 0.02 percent stronger than Tuesday's 6.1612 and within arm's reach of the base rate's record high of 6.1598 fixed on June 17. But in trading, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently acted quickly to curb expectations of yuan appreciation, traders said. "The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  has sent a clear signal that it wants to keep the yuan stable for now, having confined the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movements mainly around 6.12 over the past two or three weeks," said a dealer at a Chinese commercial bank in Shanghai. "But yuan trading volume will typically pick up near the end of a quarter, so late September will be the time to gauge how determined the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  is to maintain the yuan's stability." Traders said they believed the Chinese authorities may also want to take a wait-and-see attitude towards the yuan's value for now given a wider general trend of depreciation of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par          \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:    \par  Item                       Current   Previous  Change (pct)\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1601    6.1612      +0.02\par  Spot yuan                  6.1197    6.1200       0.00\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.66               \par  (pct)                                          \par  Spot change ytd                                +1.81\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation             +35.24\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to rise or fall 1 percent from the official midpoint rate it sets each morning. OFFSHORE CNH MARKET The offshore yuan market at a glance\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Instrument                   Current      Difference from\par                                            onshore (pct)\par  Offshore spot yuan           6.1125       +0.12*\par  Offshore non-deliverable     6.2260       -1.06**\par  forwards                                  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Premium for offshore spot over onshore **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint, since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint. . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\par     \par      RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - Yuan rally starts to fade as capital inflows to China slow\par  \par     - ANALYSIS-Bullish yuan herd leaves China fundamentals in\par the dust \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war or no, Beijing doesn't want Asia to take\par stable yuan for granted   \par     - China opens new front in money war as yuan speculation\par distorts export data \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Gap between \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint and spot rate is narrowing.\par GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qyx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qyx74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Corporate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  purchases in July show reduction in yuan\par appreciation expectations. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Hot money outflows reach record high in July GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/saz74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/saz74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange rate, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 yuan is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis