\par\par \b \uc2 China Yuan Up on Positive Economic Data, Dollar Sales\b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2013\par 11:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                    Vs Parity  Previous \par USD/CNY Central Parity   6.1729               6.1718 \par USD/CNY OTC 0830 GMT     6.1201    -0.86%     6.1206 \par             High         6.1217    -0.83% \par             Low          6.1175    -0.90% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI--China's yuan rose slightly against the U.S. dollar Wednesday after fresh economic data showed that China remains on track to post strong growth in the third quarter, and on stronger dollar sales by corporates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 On the over-the-counter market, the dollar was at CNY6.1201 around 0830 GMT, lower than Tuesday's close of CNY6.1206. It traded in a range of CNY6.1175 to CNY6.1217.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  set the dollar/yuan central parity rate at 6.1729, higher than Tuesday's 6.1718 following dollar strength overseas. The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which tracks the dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 74.574 late Tuesday in New York, higher than 74.518 late Monday. At 0830 GMT, the index was at 74.482.\par \par \uc2 The HSBC China Services Purchasing Managers' Index rose to 52.8 in August, hitting a five-month high and rising from 51.3 in July, \uc2 HSBC Holdings PLC\uc2  said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 A reading above 50 in the gauge of nationwide service-sector activity indicates on-month expansion. Wednesday's data follows a pick-up in August's manufacturing PMIs released earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 "Policymakers want the yuan to be stable, given wider uncertainties abroad, including possible U.S. military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Syria. Domestically, I don't think \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under pressure to weaken the yuan to boost exports," said a Shanghai-based trader at an Asian bank, noting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently makes only modest changes in the daily fixings.\par \par \uc2 China also wants to keep the yuan steady amid weakness in other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the trader added.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has risen 1.8% since the start of 2013.\par \par \uc2 Offshore, one-year dollar/yuan nondeliverable forward contracts fell to 6.2340/6.2380 from 6.2347/6.2384 late Tuesday, implying a 1.8% fall by the yuan over the next year.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore yuan market in Hong Kong, where the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  floats freely, the dollar was at CNY6.1143 late Wednesday, lower than CNY6.1153 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Esther Fung at esther.fung@wsj.com [ 04-09-13 0957GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1153   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130904e994000cc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
