\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CHAT: USD/CNY Steady on  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Cues, 6.1180-6.1220 Range Tipped\b0\par\par\uc2 1,495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2013\par 04:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0253 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/CNY is largely unchanged, as traders note that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is focused on keeping the yuan stable. The pair is at 6.1205 vs. 6.1206 late Tuesday. "Policymakers want the yuan to be stable given wider uncertainties abroad, including possible U.S. military \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Syria. Domestically, I don't think \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is under pressure to weaken the yuan to boost exports," says a Shanghai-based trader at an Asian bank, noting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  currently makes only modest changes in the daily fixings. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a higher central parity at 6.1729 vs. Tuesday's 6.1718. The trader tips the pair to trade between 6.1180-6.1220 range for the rest of the session. Offshore, one-year USD/CNY NDFs are at 6.2358/6.2398 from 6.2347/6.2384 late Tuesday. (esther.fung@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0224 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The 1-month USD/IDR NDF contract hits a new 4-year high of 11,775 Wednesday as the greenback rallies on strong U.S. manufacturing data. The big jump in the NDF premium to around IDR680 from IDR500 on Monday signals that spot USD/IDR, currently at 11,080, could be on a path toward 11,500 - the next big psychological resistance level. The rupiah, battered earlier this week by a record Indonesia trade deficit of $2.3 billion for July, is likely to weaken more unless the government implements further policy action in a follow-up to an impromptu rate hike last week. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0223 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The USD/JPY may trade in a narrow range before Friday's U.S. non-farm payrolls, says Junichi Ishikawa, market analyst at IG Securities in Tokyo. "The pair failed to breach the Y100 mark Tuesday, so now we may have to wait for the jobs data to gauge its next direction," he says, tipping support at 99.30 and 99.05. He says the pair is weighed by a weak Nikkei, but says thick buying offers are seen above Y99. The USD/JPY is at 99.49. (alexander.martin@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0159 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The AUD/USD jumps on 2Q GDP that was in line with expectations because it added to the view that further rate cuts are less likely, says Stuart Ive, Wellington-based senior client advisor at OM Financial. GDP climbed 0.6% in 2Q vs 1Q and was up 2.6% on a yearly basis, a government report showed. Economists had expected 0.6% on-quarter growth and a 2.5% on-year increase. Ive says the market has been repositioning itself since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday appeared to water down expectations that it will cut interest rates further and the data gave another push higher. The pair is at 0.9094 versus 0.9052 ahead of the report. He says the pair has support at 0.9030 and initial resistance at 0.9140. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar surged to as high as US$0.9087 from US$0.9050 against the greenback after the Australia's second quarter GDP came in at +2.6% on year, beating the +2.5% consensus forecast. Further upside in the Aussie/U.S. dollar pair may encounter resistance at 0.9100 and 0.9150 on its hourly chart. Spot The AUD/USD is recently at 0.9077. (jerry.tan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0144 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Crude-oil futures are down slightly in early Asia trading Wednesday after settling higher in floor trade as President Barack Obama's efforts to garner support for a military strike at Syria gained traction. "Jitters remained on western military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into Syria," ANZ Research said in a note. In the latest development, the Senate Foreign Relations Committee may vote on a military strike resolution as early as Wednesday. Oil markets will also track oil inventory data for cues. The API, an industry body, will publish its weekly statistical bulletin later Wednesday, and the U.S. EIA will publish its data on Wednesday. Nymex crude is down 31 cents at $108.23/bbl, Brent is down 11 cents at $115.57/bbl. (eric.yep@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP gaps higher at 44.60 versus its Tuesday close of 44.48, in reaction to improved U.S. ISM manufacturing data. The dollar may head back up again toward its 3-year high against the peso of 44.75. The respite in dollar strength earlier this week was short-lived after upbeat U.S manufacturing data overnight, which makes it seem more likely the Fed will taper monetary stimulus this month. Foreign investors, who were betting heavily on the peso because of the credit rating upgrades to "investment" level earlier this year, may now be rushing for the exit, fearing a mass exodus once the end of U.S. QE truly begins. The USD/PHP is recently at 44.63. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0140 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] USD/KRW rebounds to 1,102.4 recently from an earlier low of 1099.3 and late Tuesday's 1097.9 in Asia. U.S. session strength for the greenback and foreign selling of Korean stocks are pushing the pair up. Still, the won could get a lift from recent new orders for shipbuilders - who must then convert dollars back to Korean won, says Samsung Futures \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Jeon Seung-ji. The unexpected variable is the earthquake in Tokyo but the impact is too early to tell, she says. The analyst expects range trading around 1,100 for Wednesday. (jeyup.kwaak@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0138 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The dollar rose on strong U.S. ISM manufacturing data, pushing USD/MYR above the 20-day Bollinger mid and also above the psychological barrier at 3.3000, creating a mild bullish technical signal. This signal could increase in strength if the pair ends Wednesday above 3.3100 and therefore inside the Bollinger uptrend channel. The greenback got a boost from the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield rising overnight as bonds got sold off on the better-than-expected U.S manufacturing data. The ringgit may however find some support from punters betting on further action from the Malaysia government to improve the country's fiscal situation, in a follow-up to the cutting of fuel subsidies announced earlier this week. USD/MYR is now at 3.3050. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0130 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] USD/SGD's overnight rise could for now be capped by the psychological barrier at 1.2800, which is also the entrance to the Bollinger uptrend channel. The greenback spiked higher overnight on stronger U.S. manufacturing data, which adds to the likelihood that the Federal Reserve will taper quantitative easing this month. The U.S. dollar is likely to range between 1.2731 and 1.2800 for now. Singapore's August manufacturing PMI, released Tuesday, fell to 50.5 from 51.8 in July - a weaker number that, however, still reflects expansion of the sector. USD/SGD is now at 1.2781. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0108 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] CIMB upgrades the Australian banking sector to Neutral from Underweight, after lowering the risk-free rate in its discounted cash-flow assumptions to 4.25% from 5.25%, following the recent reduction in Australia's long-term expected real interest rates. "Lowering the risk-free rate we use in our DCF valuations and the removal of the discounts we applied to our multiples-based valuation (added two years ago to capture term funding price risk) pushes our price targets higher by 10-12% for the big four banks and 6-9% for the regional banks," say CIMB analysts led by John Buonaccorsi. "This is despite leaving our earnings and dividend forecasts unchanged. We also view the banks' relative valuation position versus Industrials as justified given EPS revision trends." CIMB has raised NAB (NAB.AU) to Outperform from Neutral, leaving ANZ (ANZ.AU) at Outperform, CBA (CBA.AU) at Underperform and \uc2 Westpac\uc2  (WBC.AU) at Underperform. (david.rogers1@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0048 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] A steady stream of improving Chinese economic data sent Yanzhou Coal (1171.HK) up 29% in August, its biggest one-month jump since 2009 and a much-needed boost after six months of brutal losses--shares tumbled 30% in June, for instance--amid falling coal prices. Investors may want to prepare for a dose of reality, however, as \uc2 Moody's\uc2  cuts the company's issuer rating to junk, citing Yanzhou's "weakened level of profitability," which the credit rater says is "beyond" its expectations. Shares closed Tuesday at HK$7.19, up 4.2% this week. (mia.lamar@wsj.com) [ 04-09-13 0254GMT ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130904e9940002h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
