\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ.COM What's News - Worldwide News Briefs For Aug 29\b0\par\par\uc2 719 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2013\par 19:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NORTH SEA HELICOPTER CRASH PROBE ONGOING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. air crash investigators said it was too early to identify the causes of last week's fatal helicopter crash in the U.K. North Sea. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA ARRESTS TERROR SUSPECT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian authorities said they had captured an alleged founder of the organization \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indian Mujahideen\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which is accused of carrying out bomb attacks across India that have killed dozens of people. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  REJECTS BLOC'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN CONFLICTS \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's defense minister issued a blunt rebuke to Southeast Asian counterparts, saying Beijing rejected any multilateral approach to resolving competing territorial claims in the South China Sea. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA WATCHDOG SUSPENDS REFINERY APPROVALS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's environmental regulator halted new projects at the country's two largest refining companies, a sign of stepped-up environmental scrutiny of state-owned enterprises. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA RAISES INTEREST RATES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  raised its main policy rate by a half-percentage point , reflecting a growing realization that defending the plunging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is a more pressing need than maintaining rapid economic growth. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE ECONOMY STANDS OUT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine economy grew strongly in the second quarter, underscoring how some Asian countries are riding out the emerging-markets turmoil with healthier fundamentals. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CONFIDENCE ADDS TO MOMENTUM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Business confidence in the euro zone's No. 2 and 3 economies rose in August, bolstering evidence that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  area's nascent economic recovery is gaining momentum. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GHANA COURT REJECTS ELECTION CHALLENGE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The long-running courtroom drama had served as a civics lesson for people in this still-young democracy and across Africa. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PAKISTANI CIA HELPER'S SENTENCE SET ASIDE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The prison sentence handed down to the Pakistani doctor who allegedly helped the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Central Intelligence Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  track down Osama bin Laden has apparently been overturned on appeal. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TALIBAN ATTACK U.S.-POLISH BASE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A suicide bomber was followed by heavy gunfire, killing one coalition service member and several Afghan civilians and security guards. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK OF ENGLAND READY TO DO MORE --- CARNEY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The head of the U.K. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced new measures to boost lending, but once again his message seems to have fallen on deaf ears in the markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IRAQ ATTACKS KILL SCORES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A wave of violence tore through Shiite Muslim areas in and around the Iraqi capital, killing at least 65 and wounding many more, officials said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI RUBBER FARMERS PROTEST PRICES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rubber farmers in Thailand have blockaded roads and train tracks over the past week to pressure the government to guarantee a rubber price to bolster their incomes, as it has done for rice growers. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN STUDIES PLAN TO CONTAIN RADIOACTIVE WATER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan is considering a novel approach to stem the spread of radioactive water at the crippled Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant: installing a subterranean ring of ice. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S., ASEAN DISCUSS SOUTH CHINA SEA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. and Asian defense ministers met on Wednesday to discuss initiatives aimed at reducing tensions in the South China Sea. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FIRM THAT VETTED SNOWDEN DEFENDS WORK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The private company that conducted the last background check of former NSA contractor Edward Snowden blamed the federal government for not catching any problems with its 2011 investigation of the man responsible for leaking top-secret documents. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IRAN INCREASES SOME NUCLEAR ACTIVITY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iran has prepared more than 1,000 advanced uranium-enriching machines for startup, the U.N.'s nuclear agency said Wednesday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par A BOOST FOR TASMANIA VIA ANTARCTICA? \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If elected on Sept. 7, Australia's Liberal-National coalition says it will prepare a 20-year strategic plan for research in the Antarctic region with a view to boosting struggling Tasmania's appeal as a staging point. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CROATIA MOVES TO DEFUSE EU ARREST WARRANT ROW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Croatia has moved to defuse a major clash with the EU just weeks after joining the bloc, with the country's justice minister pledging to ensure that a domestic law committing Croatia to the European arrest warrant complies with EU rules. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CYPRIOTS TRY GETTING BY WITHOUT CREDIT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More than five months since Cyprus agreed to an international bailout to avert a financial meltdown, 90% of deposits in the biggest lender remain effectively frozen while it restructures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (For continuously updated news from the Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 29, 2013 13:00 ET (17:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130829e98t003u0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
