\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ.COM What's News - Worldwide News Briefs for July 15\b0\par\par\uc2 792 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2013\par 23:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DOMESTIC CONSUMPTION DISAPPOINTS AS CHINA'S GDP SLOWS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's push to get consumers to open their wallets more and refocus the economy on domestic consumption is stalling, contributing to lower growth in the second quarter.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PUTIN HOPES SNOWDEN LEAVES RUSSIA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Russian president also reiterated that he doesn't want the situation with the NSA leaker to damage Moscow's relations with the White House.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANGLADESH PASSES NEW LABOR LAW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bangladesh passed an amended labor law, in the wake of the Rana Plaza collapse, that government officials said would herald a new era for workers' rights.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ACTIVISTS ARRESTED FOR EDF BREAK-IN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Twenty-nine Greenpeace activists were arrested after breaking into a French nuclear-power plant, the latest in a series of incidents in recent years that raise questions over the tightness of security at the country's atomic installations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HONG KONG CHANGING HOW IT HANDLES REFUGEES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Under pressure from the courts, Hong Kong is changing the way it handles its asylum seekers, as the Snowden affair has put the spotlight on the city's stringent policies for refugees.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANGLADESH SENTENCES ISLAMIST FIGURE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A tribunal investigating Bangladesh's 1971 war of independence sentenced the 91-year-old former head of the largest Islamist party to 90 years for crimes against humanity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. WANTS FINANCIAL SERVICES OFF TABLE IN EU TRADE TALKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jacob Lew\f28 \uc2 \f2  poured cold water on a push by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 's top financial markets regulator to include negotiations over financial services regulation in EU-U.S. trade talks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUNGARY ASKS IMF TO LEAVE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The IMF said it would not fill a position in Budapest as Hungarian authorities seek to reassert their sovereignty ahead of national elections next year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TURKEY SIGNALS INTEREST-RATE RISE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may throw its most powerful tool yet into the battle against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness, signaling an interest-rate rise as soon as next week after recent market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  failed to stem the lira's slide.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 'S REAL-ESTATE SECTOR SEES SOLID HOUSING DEMAND \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's real-estate sector showed strength in the first half amid solid housing demand, despite government controls on the market and slowing economic growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AFGHAN REBELS CITE MIXED MESSAGES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The botched opening of a Taliban negotiating office in Qatar hasn't created confusion just in Washington and Kabul: Insurgent field commanders on the Afghan battlefields have been befuddled by the tentative peace outreach, too.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PORTUGAL PARTIES SET PACT DEADLINE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Portugal's three main parties said that they have set a July 21 deadline to agree to a pact that would keep the country's $102 billion international rescue on track.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA ENACTS WHISTLEBLOWER LAW \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Australia legislation safeguards public servants but would enable the prosecution of anyone following the example of fugitive U.S. intelligence contractor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Edward Snowden\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BUSINESS CONFIDENCE DECLINES IN SURVEY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Businesses around the world became more gloomy about their prospects in June, an indication that they are unlikely to increase their investment spending and hiring.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CZECH EX-PREMIER ADMITS TO AFFAIR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Czech Republic's former premier this weekend said he had an affair with his top aide, a woman whose arrest in connection with an investigation into alleged bribery and abuse of power led to the collapse of his government.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BOEING\f28 \uc2 \f2  FIRE PROBE TO TAKE DAYS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global airlines continued to fly \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boeing\f28 \uc2 \f2  787 Dreamliners as investigators probed the cause of a fire that damaged one of the jets on Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BIOENERGY REVS UP IN GERMANY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A German town's experience shows how the energy sector in Europe's largest economy is being challenged by an unlikely competitor: a swarm of households and small-scale investors who are producing and selling renewable energy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ISRAEL LEADER WARNS U.S. OVER IRAN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Israeli Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Benjamin Netanyahu\f28 \uc2 \f2 , concerned that international focus on Iran's nuclear program is wavering, publicly pressed the Obama administration to take more aggressive actions against Tehran.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par METAL PLATE IS FOCUS IN FRENCH TRAIN CRASH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A 22-pound piece of metal is at the center of the investigation into Friday's train accident, which rekindled controversy over the state of the country's regional transport networks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AT LEAST 18 KILLED IN INDONESIAN BOXING MATCH RIOT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At least 18 people were killed in a stadium stampede after spectators rioted to protest a local boxer's loss in a championship match in eastern Indonesia, police said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FEARS OF NEW U.K. HOUSE PRICE BUBBLE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Weak supply means the average price of U.K. property is at an all-time high yet the government still wants to boost demand.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (For continuously updated news from the Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .) [ 07-15-13 1718ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020130715e97f000k4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
