\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan closes at record high on strong trade data; hot money suspected\b0\par\par\uc2 759 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2013\par 11:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yuan gallops to record high close of 6.1410/dlr\par \par \uc2 * Gain of 0.2 pct biggest since December 2012\par \par \uc2 * Trade surplus rebounded in April on strong export growth\par \par \uc2 * Fake trade invoices seen disguising hot money inflows\par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Gabriel Wildau\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, May 8 (Reuters) - China's yuan had its best day of the year on Wednesday after trade data showed export growth beating expectations, highlighting the possibility that firms are manipulating trade invoices in order to skirt China's capital controls and bet on yuan appreciation.\par \par \uc2 China's exports in April rose 14.7 percent from a year earlier, while imports grew 16.8 percent, leaving the country with a trade surplus of $18.16 billion for the month. That compared with a deficit of $823 million in March.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the trade data, the \uc2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 set its midpoint at its strongest level ever and sharply higher than Tuesday's fix.\par \par \uc2 Spot yuan ended at 6.1410 per dollar, its highest close ever, after touching an intraday record of 6.1396 in afternoon trade.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has rebounded sharply since Monday, when it suffered its worst day in five months after China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator released new rules to crack down on hot money inflows and fake trade invoicing.\par \par \uc2 The new rules jolted the market, with traders worrying that banks would have to buy a large amount of dollars in order to comply with new limits on long yuan positions.\par \par \uc2 But bullish yuan sentiment has now returned, with dealers saying that client demand for yuan remains significantly stronger than dollar demand.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has also gained support from expectations of policy reforms to liberalise the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Premier \uc2 Li Keqiang\uc2  told a cabinet meeting on Monday that the government would prepare an "\b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan" to achieve yuan convertibility on the capital account. Li specifically mentioned a plan for a pilot programme to allow overseas investment by individual Chinese investors.\par \par \uc2 Li's statement also boosted expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will widen the yuan's daily trading band in the coming weeks or months.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's record-high midpoint on Wednesday appeared to continue the campaign to bring the fixing closer to the spot rate, thereby preventing an abrupt one-off appreciation immediately following the band widening.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  currently allows the dollar/yuan exchange rate to diverge by no more than 1 percent from the midpoint it sets each morning.\par \par \uc2 At its closing level, the exchange rate was 0.92 percent below the midpoint, down only slightly from the 0.95 divergence that the market maintained for most of the year.\par \par \uc2 The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Item                       Current   Previous  Change (pct)\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.198     6.2083      +0.17\par Spot yuan                  6.1410    6.1541      +0.21\par Divergence from midpoint*  -0.92               \par (pct)                                          \par Spot change ytd                                +1.45\par Spot change since 2005 revaluation             +34.77\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to rise or fall 1 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each morning.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OFFSHORE CNH MARKET\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The offshore yuan market at a glance:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Instrument                   Current  Difference from onshore\par                                     (pct)\par Offshore spot yuan           6.1411     -0.00*\par Offshore non-deliverable     6.2120   -0.16**\par forwards                              \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Premium for offshore spot over onshore **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint, since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint. .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET DRIVERS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is using its daily midpoint to restrain appreciation. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/pyx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/pyx74t}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 - Corporate yuan purchases reflect heightened yuan appreciation expectations or at least a reduction in long dollar positions. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/syx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/syx74t}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 - Hot money inflows return with a vengeance GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/raz74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/raz74t}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange rate, the yuan is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Yuan speculators muddle \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's exports\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  returns to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid heavy capital inflows\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war or no, Beijing doesn't want Asia to take stable yuan for granted\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - China eyes market forces to drive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Sanjeev Miglani)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-CLOSE/ | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130511e9580003b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
