\par\par \b \uc2 Kiwi dlr falls on rare RBNZ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , Aussie off lows on  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  data\b0\par\par\uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2013\par 00:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Kiwi dlr down 0.6 pct vs USD, yen, euro\par \par \uc2 * Aussie relieved by China upbeat trade data\par \par \uc2 * Aussie up 1-1/2 cents on NZD\par \par \uc2 By Gyles Beckford and Cecile Lefort\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY/WELLINGTON, May 8 (Reuters) - The kiwi dollar retreated on Wednesday after the head of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try and restrain the strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though traders doubted it would blunt its longer-term trend.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar fell as much as three quarters of a cent to $0.8362 after a slew of comments from \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand\uc2  (RBNZ) Governor \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2 , before steadying at $0.8400.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief confirmed to a parliamentary committee that the RBNZ had sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though he did not expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have a material impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The remarks came on top of earlier warnings made by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  against increasing risks from high house prices and a strong kiwi dollar.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi was 0.6 percent lower on the day, showing a loss of 1.5 percent since Monday.\par \par \uc2 "This is significant, but we expect the drop in the NZ dollar will be short-lived," said Westpac chief economist Dominick Stephens.\par \par \uc2 He said he backed Wheeler's view that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have a short-term impact by taking the tops off rallies.\par \par \uc2 Support was seen at $0.8376, the 100-day MA. It has lost 1.5 pct since Monday.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi was nursing large losses against the euro, yen and pound. It even lost ground to its Aussie cousin which had been hit hard on Tuesday after the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  cut rates to a record low of 2.75 percent.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie jumped 1-1/2 cent to NZ$1.2122, from NZ$1.1965, its lowest since 2009.\par \par \uc2 AUSSIE OFF LOWS\par \par \uc2 The Aussie came off two-month lows to last trade at $1.0183\par \par \uc2 after China posted stronger-than-expected trade numbers, though some analysts felt the figures were inflated by speculative capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 The upbeat reading helped ease some of the fears about an economic slowdown in the Asian giant. Australia is very sensitive to news out of China, its top export market.\par \par \uc2 A breakdown of the data showed Beijing increased the country's imports from Australia by 11 percent in April, auguring well for the economy Down Under.\par \par \uc2 Also helping was a rebound in iron ore <.IO62-CNI=SI> prices to $130 a tonne. The commodity, Australia's largest export earner, has skidded 10 percent so far this year but still remained elevated.\par \par \uc2 "The Aussie is holding up above lows...and I would not be surprised if it grinded higher as it is still a high yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Greg Gibbs, a strategist at \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Aussie has slipped more than 1 percent on the week with investors speculating that more interest rate cuts were in the cards.\par \par \uc2 Interbank futures <0#YIB:> show markets have fully priced a cut to 2.5 percent by August.\par \par \uc2 Immediate support was seen at $1.0150, where traders cite option barriers, ahead of $1.0116, a March trough. Resistance was found around $1.0250.\par \par \uc2 Australian government debt softened after recent hefty gains. The three-year bond future contract gave back 0.010 points to 97.510, having climbed to a six-month peak of 97.550 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 A sustained break above 97.520 would open the way to 97.749, the highest since early October.\par \par \uc2 Three-year bond yields hovered around 2.505 percent, having troughed to 2.480 percent.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year futures contract shed 0.045 points to 96.890.\par \par \uc2 New Zealand government bonds was a touch firmer with yields one basis point lower.\par \par \uc2 (Australia and New Zealand bureaux; Editing by Kim Coghill)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-NEWZEALAND/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2) | AUF | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ND | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130510e9570016x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
