\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan closes at record high for third day\b0\par\par\uc2 By Pete Sweeney   \par \uc2 767 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2013\par 11:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, April 16 (Reuters) - The yuan closed at another record high against the dollar for the third straight day on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set an unusually strong midpoint, but traders in the offshore market are signalling they think the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to peak.\par \par \uc2 Traders in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market initially attributed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's string of aggressive midpoint settings to a visit by U.S. Secretary of State John Kerry, but Kerry has since left China and yet the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  continues to signal permission for the spot yuan to scale fresh heights.\par \par \uc2 Ordinarily the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sets the midpoint inversely to overnight moves in the dollar index to keep the rate stable, but the midpoint rose on Tuesday even though the dollar index also climbed overnight.\par \par \uc2 The move also flies in the face of predictions that Beijing would devalue the yuan alongside the Japanese yen after the Japanese government embarked on an economic stimulus programme that saw the yen lose nearly a quarter of its value against the dollar in the past six months.\par \par \uc2 Some traders theorized that the strong midpoint settings are intended as a gesture at recent pessimistic moves by foreign ratings agencies questioning China's management of its local debt.\par \par \uc2 However, Robert Minikin, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered in Hong Kong, said the strong midpoint setting was to be expected given moves in the Japanese yen market against the dollar, which saw the yen strengthen in overnight trade before staging another correction during day trade on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Minikin did allow for political factors in the U.S. continuing to exercise influence.\par \par \uc2 "We've got the G20 meeting next week and also we have the release of the semi-annual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report from the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 . The combination of these few things going on makes it a bit more attractive to move the dollar-CNY fix lower (stronger) at this point."\par \par \uc2 Minikin and other traders believe the market will begin to weaken in the near future.\par \par \uc2 China has seen a dramatic resurgence of speculative hot money inflows from overseas markets in recent months, which has complicated its monetary policy and made China's exports more expensive.\par \par \uc2 A trader in Shanghai told Reuters that corporates were still eagerly unloading \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, even in the face of mixed economic data that showed China's GDP grew more slowly than expected in the first quarter. The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Item                       Current   Previous  Change \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint                6.2408    6.2454       +0.07%\par Spot yuan                    6.1831    6.1871       +0.06%\par Divergence from midpoint*    -0.92%                       \par Spot change ytd              +0.69%                       \par Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 +33.77%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to rise or fall 1 percent from the official midpoint rate it sets each morning.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OFFSHORE CNH MARKET\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The offshore spot yuan (CNH) market has reversed itself in the past two days. Where CNH was been trading at a premium to the onshore version since February, offshore market flipped over to the discount side on Monday, indicating offshore traders no longer expect much more in the way of appreciation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par Instrument                   Current   Difference from onshore\par Offshore spot yuan           6.1875    *-0.07%\par Offshore non-deliverable     6.2535    **-0.20%\par forwards                               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Premium for offshore spot over onshore. **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint, since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint. .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET DRIVERS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Hot money inflows return with a vengeance GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/saz74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/saz74t}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 - Corporate yuan purchases reflect heightened yuan appreciation expectations or at least a reduction in long dollar positions. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/syx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/syx74t}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange rate, the yuan is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ANALYSIS: Yuan speculators muddle \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's exports, complicating reform\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  returns to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid heavy capital inflows\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war or no, Beijing doesn't want Asia to take stable yuan for granted\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - China eyes market forces to drive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Sanjeev Miglani)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-CLOSE/ | ABN | D | E | RBN | C | GRO | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z | MTL | SOF | RNP | DNP | PTD | PCM   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130419e94g000eo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
