\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan equals record high, then pulls back on \uc2 PBOC\uc2  stability push\b0\par\par\uc2 773 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 05:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yuan opens at record high 6.2095/dlr\par \par \uc2 * Mild \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen to pull rate weaker than 6.21\par \par \uc2 * Market pressure supports yuan appreciation\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 PBOC\uc2  favors stability amid macro-economic uncertainty\par \par \uc2 By Gabriel Wildau\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, March 29 (Reuters) - China's yuan on Friday equaled a record high set two days earlier, but appears headed for only a tiny gain on the week as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears intent on holding the yuan steady.\par \par \uc2 Spot yuan opened at a record-high 6.2195 per dollar, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at around 6.2104 near midday, with traders seeing signs that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  as necessary to hold the exchange rate above the psychologically significant 6.21 resistance level.\par \par \uc2 At current levels, the yuan is up 0.03 percent on the week.\par \par \uc2 Before trading began, the \uc2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 set its daily midpoint at 6.2689, 0.08 percent stronger than Thursday and the strongest fix since May 2012.\par \par \uc2 Back then the spot rate was around 6.30 and caught in a weakening trend. Unlike now, the spot yuan was also consistently trading at the bottom end of the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's daily allowable trading band, so the strong fixings served to prevent the spot rate from weakening even further.\par \par \uc2 By contrast, market pressure has kept the yuan near the top of its trading band since September, and the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  is using relatively weak midpoints to prevent excessive appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The strong midpoint on Friday came in response to a fall in the dollar index overnight. The index tracks the dollar's value against a basket of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighted towards the euro.\par \par \uc2 The euro hovered near four-month lows against the dollar on Friday, beset by political deadlock in Italy and worries huge losses Cypriot depositors have been forced to stomach as part of a bailout could unnerve investors in other euro zone debt.\par \par \uc2 Traders expect the yuan to fluctuate in a narrow range around 6.21 in the weeks ahead, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintaining a wait-and-see stance amid lingering fears of an Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war and uncertainty whether strong export growth seen early this year will continue.\par \par \uc2 Both of those factors could cause the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  to guide the yuan weaker. But the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  has also expressed concern about a possible resurgence of inflation this year. If inflation ticks up, that could cause the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  to unleash further gains in the yuan.\par \par \uc2 Most analysts are maintaining their forecasts from the start of the year that the yuan will rise by 1 to 2 percent overall in 2013, placing it around 6.14 at year-end. The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Item                       Current   Previous  Change (pct)\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.2689    6.2742      +0.08%\par Spot yuan                  6.2104    6.2143      +0.06%\par Divergence from midpoint*  -0.93%              \par Spot change ytd                                +0.32%\par Spot change since 2005 revaluation             +33.27%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to rise or fall 1 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each morning.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OFFSHORE CNH MARKET\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par Instrument                 Current     Difference from\par                                      onshore (pct)\par Offshore spot yuan         6.2065      *0.06%\par        (pct)                         \par Offshore non-deliverable   6.301       **-0.51%\par forwards                               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Premium for offshore spot over onshore **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint, since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint. .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MARKET DRIVERS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is using its daily midpoint to restrain further appreciation. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/pyx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/pyx74t}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 - Corporate yuan purchases reflect heightened yuan appreciation expectations or at least a reduction in long dollar positions. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/syx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/syx74t}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 - Hot money inflows, which should support yuan appreciation, returned in Jan following nine straight months of outflows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/raz74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/raz74t}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange rate, the yuan is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  returns to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid heavy capital inflows\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  restrains yuan rise in response to Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - China eyes market forces to drive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reform\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Bank of China extends yuan deposits to promote redback's rise\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Matt Driskill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-MIDDAY/ | ABN | D | E | RBN | C | GRO | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z | MTL | SOF | RNP | DNP | PTD | PCM   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130401e93t0003t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
