\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-China  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  eyes reform, more flexible yuan in 2013\b0\par\par\uc2 1,035 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 22:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * China to push ahead with reform, promote \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility-PBOC dep gov\par \par \uc2 * Yuan close to equilibrium level - \uc2 PBOC\uc2  dep gov\par \par \uc2 * Qianhai \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  pilot could be ready in H1 2013 - NDRC chief\par \par \uc2 (Adds band widening in paragraphs 5-8)\par \par \uc2 BEIJING, March 6 (Reuters) - China will press ahead with reforms to allow more flexibility in the yuan's exchange rate and the remaining barriers to creating a cross-border \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading zone could be cleared in the first half of this year, senior officials said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Yi Gang, deputy governor of the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 , reiterated Beijing's commitment to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform on the sidelines of the annual meeting of China's parliament, the National People's Congress.\par \par \uc2 "We will continue to reform and open up. I'm confident that the renminbi (yuan) exchange rate will be more balanced and flexible and basically stable," Yi, who also heads the \uc2 State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SAFE), China's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchdog, told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Sources with knowledge of the latest \uc2 PBOC\uc2  thinking have told Reuters that China is set to use swelling offshore holdings of its tightly managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth around 1 trillion yuan ($160 billion) to justify a landmark shift in tactics to relax capital controls.\par \par \uc2 "Exchange rate reform is not to be found in the rate or the volume, but in the evolving exchange rate mechanism," Wu Xiaoling, a former deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, told reporters.\par \par \uc2 But she rejected the idea of broadening the yuan trading band beyond the current 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 "I think 1 percent is enough. It doesn't preclude a future widening, but under the current economic uncertainty, keeping the exchange rate appropriately stable is good for the Chinese and the world economies."\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, influential Chinese economist Yu Yongding called for a widening of the yuan trading band this year to 3 percent, or even as much as 7 percent, to give the market a greater role in setting the rate.\par \par \uc2 Zhang Ping, head of the \uc2 National Development and Reform Commission\uc2  (NDRC), the country's top economic planning agency, meanwhile told an NPC news conference that plans for China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading pilot programme were progressing smoothly.\par \par \uc2 Zhang said only six of 22 measures needed to get a $45 billion special economic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading zone up and running in Qianhai, near the border with Hong Kong, were outstanding and likely to be resolved in the first half of 2013.\par \par \uc2 "We are hopeful of coming up with plans to solve those problems in the first half of this year," Zhang said.\par \par \uc2 Outstanding issues included ones related to legal practices, given differences in the judicial systems of the mainland and Hong Kong - a special administrative region of China governed under the principle of "one country, two systems".\par \par \uc2 China set up the Qianhai business zone offering freer \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements and Hong Kong professional standards last June. The government released rules in December for companies that incorporate in the area to borrow yuan from Hong Kong banks with interest rates and tenors to be fixed independently.\par \par \uc2 RISING YUAN DEMAND\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's Yi also remarked that the yuan was close to its equilibrium level and reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's assertion that it had cut \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Both points emphasise the stability that Chinese policymakers want to ensure even as they try turn the yuan into a more freely traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Official remarks that the yuan is near its equilibrium contrast with data this week suggesting that demand for the yuan may be rising again as China recovers from last year's economic downturn, the worst in 13 years.\par \par \uc2 The yuan hit a seven-week high on Wednesday, a day after data from the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  showed \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commercial banks bought a record 683.7 billion yuan ($109.9 billion) worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January.\par \par \uc2 Economists say the all-time high purchase indicates capital is flowing back into China, although \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Zhou Xiaochuan\uc2  downplayed the idea when asked on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "You can't draw any conclusions from one month's data. The volume every day is very high," said Zhou, also speaking on the sidelines of parliament. "Sometimes there is more demand for renminbi and sometimes for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Large \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases by \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commercial banks amount to base money creation and can fuel inflation unless the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  soaks up the excess yuan injected into the system via sterilisation.\par \par \uc2 In reference to that, Yi said China would use open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  including purchase agreements and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bills to mop up excess liquidity stemming from \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows.\par \par \uc2 SAFE had said last month that China faces greater risks in capital inflows and outflows this year, against a backdrop of economic uncertainty worldwide.\par \par \uc2 Ting Lu\uc2 , an economist at Bank of America-Merrill Lynch, said the record purchases of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January showed pent-up demand for the yuan as confidence in the world's second-largest economy rebounds.\par \par \uc2 But Lu said he did not think large \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases would be sustained as the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  has clearly signalled that there is little room for the yuan to rise further.\par \par \uc2 "The room for further yuan appreciation against the dollar is limited, as is signalled by the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's declarations that it has reduced its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers say they still spot aggressive buying or selling of dollars by authorities.\par \par \uc2 China wants to turn the yuan into a convertible, or less controlled, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that becomes a major medium of exchange in global commerce and one day would rival the dollar as an alternative investment in government reserves.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 6.2209 Chinese yuan)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Yao, Steven Bian, Lucy Hornby, Zhang Shengnan and Cao Weihao; Writing by Koh Gui Qing; Editing by Nick Edwards and Nick Macfie)\par \par \uc2 CHINA-ECONOMY/YUAN (UPDATE 3) | ABN | C | GRO | MTL | SOF | D | E | RBN | G | M | O | OIL | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z | RNP | DNP | PGE | PCM | PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130305e9350014z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
