\par\par \b \uc2 China wades cautiously into Asian " \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  war", reins in yuan\b0\par\par\uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2013\par 10:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * China c.bank has restrained yuan rise since mid-Jan\par \par \uc2 * Traders see appreciation pressure on corporate demand\par \par \uc2 * But \uc2 PBOC\uc2  favours stability amid "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war" uncertainty\par \par \uc2 * C.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  revives despite market reform rhetoric\par \par \uc2 By Gabriel Wildau\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Feb 5 (Reuters) - Chinese authorities have responded to the dramatic fall in the Japanese yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks by tightening their grip on the yuan and beating back market pressure for the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly stated its intention to reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and market trends have borne out such rhetoric for much of the last year.\par \par \uc2 But the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  (PBOC) \uc2 has stepped up its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks to head off yuan appreciation amid fears its Asian neighbors may resort to competitive devaluations to bolster their exports.\par \par \uc2 "In characteristic \uc2 PBOC\uc2  fashion, when things are uncertain and unclear, they basically keep dollar/renminbi within a range," said Claudio Piron, head of emerging Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fixed-income strategy at \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a break with typical practice, the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  has guided the yuan slightly weaker over the last two weeks, despite a fall in the dollar versus the euro.\par \par \uc2 Typically the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  sets stronger midpoints in response to a fall in the dollar index, which tracks the greenback's value against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The basket is heavily weighted towards the euro.\par \par \uc2 Analysts and traders say the break with precedent is a response to the recent decline in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The yen\par \par \uc2 fell 16.9 percent from October through Monday, while the Korean won dropped 3.6 percent from Jan 15 through Monday.\par \par \uc2 After touching a record high of 6.2124 versus the dollar on Jan 14, spot yuan fell 0.35 percent to a 2013 low of 6.2342 on Monday, though it had recovered somewhat to 6.2294 by Tuesday's close.\par \par \uc2 Chinese traders say the recent depreciation has occurred despite robust corporate demand for yuan.\par \par \uc2 "Client orders for yuan are still pretty large, and there is still appreciation pressure. But the midpoint seems to be following Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with short-term depreciation," said a trader at a large commercial bank in Shanghai.\par \par \uc2 In addition to using the midpoint, the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  has stepped up its direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since early December. Traders have consistently reported large dollar purchases by state banks that they suspect are being conducted on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  is back to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - to the net tune of USD 34bn in Q4 2012," Standard Chartered economist \uc2 Stephen Green\uc2  wrote in a note to clients on Monday.\par \par \uc2 In a market with average daily volume of nearly $14 billion in the first three quarters of 2012, such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is far from overwhelming.\par \par \uc2 But a few days of large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in mid-December sent a clear signal to the market that the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  will not tolerate overly rapid appreciation. Once expectations for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  become entrenched, traders police themselves.\par \par \uc2 "Market positioning is relatively cautious right now. Everyone is guessing when (the big banks) will come out to buy (dollars) and how much they will buy," said the Chinese bank trader.\par \par \uc2 Most analysts still appreciate moderate appreciation for full-year 2013, but at a slow pace.\par \par \uc2 Standard Chartered predicts the yuan will rise 2.1 percent for full-year 2013, reaching 6.10 at year-end. \uc2 HSBC\uc2  is less bullish, predicting an 0.8 percent gain to 6.18. Most other forecasts fall within this range.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Li Wenke; Editing by Kim Coghill)\par \par \uc2 CHINA-YUAN/\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCYWAR\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z | E | RBN | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130205e925000ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
