\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -China, US data help Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  to weekly gains; up vs yen\b0\par\par\uc2 1,277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2013\par 08:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Baht up 1.7 pct vs dlr for week, rupee gains 1.5 pct\par \par \uc2 * Won hits near 3-yr high to yen\par \par \uc2 * Stock inflows, speculators support Philippine peso\par \par \uc2 * Taiwan dlr up on exporters, foreign financial inflows\par \par \uc2 * Rupee gains on equity-linked inflows; corporate dlr demand eases\par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Jan 18 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Friday, to head for weekly gains, with the Philippine peso near a five-year peak, as more evidence of recovery in the world's top two economies brightened the outlook for the region and bolstered risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended gains against the yen on expectations for the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  to take bold steps to loosen monetary conditions, including further quantitative easing, at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's meeting on Monday and Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The South Korean won hit a near three-year high against the yen.\par \par \uc2 The peso gained on stock inflows and demand from speculators who see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gaining further based on sustained inflows and stronger economic fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar advanced on exporters and foreign financial inflows.\par \par \uc2 Even the Indonesian rupiah, which has been under pressure due to fears over its trade deficit and outflows from the domestic bond market, rose on equity-linked inflows and as corporate dollar demand eased, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "Risk sentiment looks good with good U.S. data. China data also helps and BOJ's QE seems (likely to be) aggressive too. So Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  can stay strong," said \uc2 BNP Paribas\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Thio Chin Loo in Singapore, referring to the Bank of Japan's quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 The won and the peso, the best performing emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of 2012, will lead appreciation in the regional units, she added.\par \par \uc2 China's economy grew 7.9 percent in the fourth quarter from a year earlier, slightly exceeding market expectations. December industrial output and retail sales also topped forecasts, providing more signs of recovery in the world's second-largest economy.\par \par \uc2 They came after healthy U.S. labor and housing data indicated sustained improvement in the U.S. economy, Asia's main export market.\par \par \uc2 In addition to optimism over the economies, investors expect more liquidity to support emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were to set to see weekly gains, led by the Thai baht.\par \par \uc2 The baht has gained 1.7 percent against the dollar so far this week, according to Thomson Reuters data, on continuous inflows to the country's stocks and bonds.\par \par \uc2 If the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds onto the rise, it would be it would be the largest weekly percentage appreciation since early December 2011, the data showed.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee has followed the baht with a 1.5 percent rise against the greenback so far this week, according to the data, as investors expect a hike in diesel prices to improve the country's fiscal deficit.\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar and the Malaysian ringgit have advanced 0.3 percent to the dollar, respectively. The peso has edged higher.\par \par \uc2 Still, some analysts said regional units are unlikely to extend gains further as \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic recovery has been factored in. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caution also stayed intact.\par \par \uc2 Jonathan Cavenagh, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2  in Singapore, reckoned emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were unlikely to extend gains at least in the near term, adding the won, the Philippine peso and the ringgit may see some corrections.\par \par \uc2 Long positions in most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have already decreased, although bullish bets on the baht and the ringgit reached their highest levels in the past two weeks, a Reuters poll showed on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won hit 11.7005 to the yen, its strongest since April 2010. If the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthens past the previous peak of 11.6872, it may head to 10.8670, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 It also gained against the dollar on strong data from the United States and China.\par \par \uc2 But the won gave up some of initial gains as importers' covered short dollar positions before the weekend, to trade around 1,057.2 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Investors tend to think the won will rise without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But they may see some corrections, especially if it keeps staying weaker than mid-1,050 (level to the dollar) and we don't see big demand from exporters or offshore funds," said a foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2 The peso strengthened to 40.55 per dollar, a notch weaker than Tuesday's high of 40.54, the strongest since February 2008.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  found support from stock inflows and demand from interbank speculators who expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gain on continued inflows and positive economic fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 Some investors ,including leveraged names, reduced long positions in the peso after China's GDP data, saying the optimism on the world's second-largest economy had been at least partly factored in.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying dollars around 40.55, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 But the peso was seen staying firm, they added.\par \par \uc2 "Dollar/peso will remain heavy as lack of client demand put pressure on the downside," said a foreign bank dealer in Manila, adding it may head to 40.50 although it could weaken to 40.65 on possible further dollar short-covering.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The rupiah's indicative prices gained 0.1 percent to 9,630 per dollar while its traded levels were around 9,850, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 But the traded levels were firmer than recent real market prices around 9,900 with some equity-linked inflows and short-term investors' bids, they added.\par \par \uc2 Dollar demand from local importers eased, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 In forwards market, the rupiah advanced on global risk appetite with one-month dollar/rupiah non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) down 0.2 percent to 9,850.\par \par \uc2 TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar advanced on foreign financial inflows and exporters' demand for settlements.\par \par \uc2 The island's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  found little support from the \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's growth figure amid caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Some foreign financial institutions and importers bought the\par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar, they added.\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar is expected to appreciate further due to stock inflows next week, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 But it may face resistance at around 28.800 to the greenback with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying dollars, they added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0645 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        90.13          89.84       -0.32\par  Sing dlr        1.2253         1.2239       -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      28.950         29.085       +0.47\par  Korean won     1057.35        1058.10       +0.07\par  Baht             29.76          29.76       +0.00\par  Peso             40.59          40.63       +0.11\par  Rupiah         9630.00        9642.00       +0.12\par  Rupee            53.96          54.39       +0.79\par  Ringgit         3.0106         3.0160       +0.18\par  Yuan            6.2150         6.2160       +0.02\par  Change so far in 2013\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        90.13          86.79       -3.71\par  Sing dlr        1.2253         1.2219       -0.28\par  Taiwan dlr      28.950         29.136       +0.64\par  Korean won     1057.35        1070.60       +1.25\par  Baht             29.76          30.61       +2.86\par  Peso             40.59          41.05       +1.15\par  Rupiah         9630.00        9630.00       +0.00\par  Rupee            53.96          54.99       +1.91\par  Ringgit         3.0106         3.0580       +1.57\par  Yuan            6.2150         6.2303       +0.25\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1) | ABX | ABN | D | E | RBN | IF | J | M | PHD | SI | SNI | SNS | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130121e91i000c2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex10