\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan closes just shy of record after eight-month high c.bank fix\b0\par\par\uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2013\par 10:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yuan closes 0.09 pct firmer at 6.2241/dlr\par \par \uc2 * C.bank sets strongest yuan fix since May 2012\par \par \uc2 * Stronger fix is response to overnight fall in dollar index\par \par \uc2 * Possible sign that c.bank will tolerate mild appreciation\par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Gabriel Wildau\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Jan 8 (Reuters) - \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its strongest midpoint in eight months on Tuesday after a fall in the dollar the day before, pushing the yuan within a hair's breadth of its all-time high and raising the prospect of further appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The yuan changed hands at 6.2227 per dollar in mid-afternoon, just shy of late November's record high of 6.2223. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated slightly to close at 6.2241 for a gain of 0.09 percent from Monday's close.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's midpoint of 6.2804 set before the start of trade on Tuesday was its strongest since May 2012, although only 0.1 percent stronger than Monday's fix of 6.2872.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 allows the exchange rate to rise or fall as much as 1 percent from the midpoint it sets each morning.\par \par \uc2 The stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixing came in response to an overnight fall in the dollar against the euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as investors anticipate a continuation of easy monetary policy from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  typically fixes the yuan firmer when the dollar index falls overnight. But traders said Tuesday's unusually strong response to the latest fall may also signal the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's willingness to permit some yuan appreciation following six weeks during which authorities capped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stated repeatedly that it intends to reduce its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 With signs that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic recovery is on firm footing while inflation may be on the rebound, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may now be more comfortable allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate.\par \par \uc2 But traders caution that a single day's strong midpoint is not enough to conclude that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is shifting tack.\par \par \uc2 The yuan hit the upper limit of its daily trading band nearly every day in November and early December, when steady midpoint settings curbed the yuan's advance, and this created a deadlock during which trading volume evaporated with dollar bids absent from the market.\par \par \uc2 Only when major state banks - apparently acting on behalf of the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  - stepped in to buy dollars in mid-December did liquidity return to the market.\par \par \uc2 Although the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  is no longer \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on such a large scale, most traders believe that major state banks are still standing guard, buying dollars as necessary to keep the yuan clear of its top-end limit.\par \par \uc2 Although such views are impossible to confirm, traders note how the exchange rate has remained close to the band's limit without actually touching it.\par \par \uc2 Allowing resumed appreciation by setting a stronger midpoint would relieve the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  and state banks from the burden of maintaining market liquidity while keeping the exchange rate inside the band.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Jacqueline Wong and Edmund Klamann)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-CLOSE/ | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130111e918000kw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
