\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan flat, market keeps eye on U.S. budget talks\b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2012\par 06:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Spot rate, midpoint flatten out alongside dollar\par \par \uc2 * Trade volume at $4.878 billion by midday\par \par \uc2 * Optimism about U.S. fiscal cliff supports yuan\par \par \uc2 * Offshore forwards forecast depreciation in 2013\par \par \uc2 By Pete Sweeney\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Dec 18 (Reuters) - China's yuan was flat in morning trade on Tuesday in moderate volume as global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets awaited signs of progress on the U.S. "fiscal cliff" impasse.\par \par \uc2 The yuan changed hands at 6.2306 per dollar at midday, 0.07 percent firmer than Monday's close.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also held its official midpoint stable at 6.2880 per dollar, barely changed from Monday's fix of 6.2892.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 allows the exchange rate to rise or fall 1 percent from the midpoint it sets each morning.\par \par \uc2 Trading volume stood at $4.878 billion at midday, compared to around $2 billion at the same time on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which the yuan usually tracks inversely while moving in sympathy with the euro, declined slightly in overnight trade.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has been sliding in global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since mid-November as risk appetite increased even as the U.S. government embarked on a fourth round of monetary easing.\par \par \uc2 Expectations that the world's largest economy would successfully negotiate itself out of a fiscal deadlock before the end of the year have increased risk appetite, pushing investors into the euro and other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This, combined with domestic factors, has supported bullish sentiment in the domestic yuan market, but traders said they expect sentiment to moderate in 2013.\par \par \uc2 Offshore yuan one-year non-deliverable forward contracts (NDFs) have flattened out in December but continue to imply depreciation in the next twelve months, quoted at 6.3120 at midday.\par \par \uc2 Offshore spot yuan (CNH=D3) continues to trade at a premium to onshore yuan, at 6.2095 to the dollar, as it has since the beginning of December. The premium supports theories that the onshore value of the yuan is being suppressed by backstage \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CHINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -YUAN-MIDDAY/ | ABN | D | E | RBN | C | GRO | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z | MTL | SOF | RNP | DNP | PTD | PCM   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121221e8ci00069\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
