\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2012\par 01:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par         Immediate Range    Larger Range \par  \par    USD/CNY 6.2500-6.2582   6.2400-6.2646 \par    USD/TWD 29.035-29.140   29.000-29.200 \par    USD/KRW  1,070-1,079     1,068-1,083 \par    USD/SGD 1.2200-1.2215   1.2171-1.2228 \par    USD/MYR 3.0435-3.0500   3.0350-3.0555 \par    USD/THB  30.56-30.62     30.50-30.69 \par    USD/PHP  40.98-41.00     40.85-41.20 \par    USD/IDR  9,620-9,635     9,600-9,650 \par    USD/INR  54.15-54.50     54.00-55.00 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- slight upside bias. While the USD may have slipped again after the FOMC meeting Wednesday, USD/CNY could remain well-supported and possibly even rise slightly, lifted by PBOC \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was once again suspected to have been buying dollars in the spot market towards the end of Wednesday, as they have been doing the whole of this week. The market could be reaching the point where speculative traders start to turn long USD/CNY, on expectations that the PBOC could push USD/CNY even higher by the end of the week. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate resistance is at 6.2582 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 6.2646 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2700 (psychological resistance). Immediate support for USD/CNY is at 6.2500 (psychological support), then at 6.2453 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 6.2400 (psychological support).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- downside bias. USD/TWD could drop to the bottom of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 29.035 on the back of the USD weakening after the U.S. Fed announced a continuation of monetary easing through additional bond buying to expand their balance sheet. The pair could test the 29.000 psychological support soon if USD-selling accelerates on improving risk appetite; USD/TWD could fall sharply on stop-loss orders triggered under 29.000. Dow Jones technical analysis shows initial support is at 29.035 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 29.000 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 29.140 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.200 (psychological resistance), before 29.230 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- consolidation with downside bias. USD/KRW may be targeting the 1,070 psychological floor next as the greenback slumps after the dovish outcome of the FOMC meeting Wednesday. More weakness lies ahead for USD/KRW if the pair triggers sell stop-loss orders likely waiting under 1,070. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1,070 (psychological support), before 1,068 (bottom of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,079 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,080 (psychological resistance), before 1,083 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- consolidation with downside bias. USD/SGD remains supported around the psychological level of 1.2200, even after the USD selloff that the FOMC meeting triggered. Market chatter is that the MAS could be actively supporting USD/SGD to slow the pace of SGD appreciation. USD/SGD could thus be stuck in a fairly narrow 1.2200-1.2228 range, capped by the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance which is likely to be a tough level to break. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2200 (psychological support), then at 1.2193 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2171 (bottom of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2215 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 1.2228 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 1.2237 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- downside bias. USD/MYR may soon display more bearish bias if it falls further, under the weight of the heavy USD post-FOMC meeting, and enters the daily Bollinger downtrend channel which begins at 3.0435. USD bears are likely to pounce on the dovish tone of the U.S. Fed and attempt to push USD/MYR lower, which may lead to triggering of sell stop-loss orders. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.0435 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.0400 (psychological support), before 3.0350 (bottom of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.0500 (psychological resistance), then at 3.0515 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 3.0555 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- downside bias. USD/THB may head lower in the short-term, after the pair dropped into the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 30.62. The channel is likely to guide the pair toward the psychological support at 30.50. A generally weaker USD is driving this move lower, after the FOMC unveiled an expansion of the Fed's bond-buying program to replace \b \highlight22\uc2 Operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  Twist. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.56 (bottom of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 30.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 30.62 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.67 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 30.69 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- consolidation with downside bias. USD/PHP is likely to gap lower at the open and start the day under the psychological barrier at 41.00, after the U.S. FOMC decision to continue bond purchases into 2013 depressed the USD. The pair could fall back into the daily Bollinger downtrend channel in a knee-jerk reaction to the FOMC's dovish stance, which sank the dollar broadly and is helping to boost risk appetite. If USD/PHP closes the day under 40.98 and therefore back inside the Bollinger downtrend channel, more weakness could follow. However, despite the overall weaker USD, traders have been wary of BSP \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently, which could thus support USD/PHP. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 40.98 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 40.85 (BSP \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level), before 40.75 (bottom of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 41.00 (psychological resistance and), before 41.20 (psychological resistance and 20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- consolidation. In spite of the generally softer USD after the FOMC unveiled plans to expand its balance sheet by buying $45 billion of Treasurys a month, USD/IDR may remain well-bid due to onshore corporate demand into the year-end, says a dealer. The pair has so far this week remained resilient against downside USD pressure, and could remain supported once again. Technical support levels near 9,600-9,605 are also helping to prop up USD/IDR. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support lies at 9,620 (bottom of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 9,605 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support and 20-day Bollinger mid), then at 9,600 (psychological support), before 9,585 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel ). Immediate resistance is at 9,635 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,650 (intra-week high).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- consolidation with downside bias. USD/INR may have a temporary base near 54.00-54.15 where the 20-day Bollinger mid support and the psychological barrier at 54.00 form a fairly broad support zone. But the pair could eventually breach this as the dollar retreats further after the dovish FOMC outcome. As long as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  continues to pump money into the U.S. economy, the greenback has little chance of rallying for now. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 54.15 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 54.00 (psychological support), before 53.69 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 54.50 (psychological resistance), then at 55.00 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 13-12-12 0039GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121213e8cd0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
