\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan ends up; c.bank seen injecting liquidity to relieve deadlock\b0\par\par\uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2012\par 11:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * C.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen to provide dollar demand\par \par \uc2 * Closes weaker than top-end limit for first time this week\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 PBOC\uc2  appears to help banks unload long dollar positions\par \par \uc2 * But yuan still firmer than Thurs on stronger c.bank fix\par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 By Gabriel Wildau\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The yuan closed below its top-end limit for the first time this week on Friday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost liquidity after a week of anemic volumes.\par \par \uc2 The yuan closed at 6.2267 per dollar, marginally firmer than Thursday's close of 6.2281.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last half hour of trade, breathing life into a market that had been virtually paralysed for weeks due to a lack of dollar buyers.\par \par \uc2 The closing level was four pips weaker than the strongest level allowed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily midpoint. \uc2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 allows the exchange rate to rise or fall 1 percent from the midpoint it sets each morning.\par \par \uc2 Dollar bids were nowhere to be seen this week as the 1 percent band prevented dealers from quoting prices that would attract would-be buyers. The yuan had hit its limit for 24 of the last 27 sessions.\par \par \uc2 The deadlock continued through Friday morning, as the spot rate stayed glued to Friday's limit until about 4:00 p.m. China time (0800 GMT).\par \par \uc2 But volume surged in the last 30 minutes of trade, as traders said dollar bids suddenly re-appeared.\par \par \uc2 Daily turnover on Friday totaled $13.9 billion following a week in which it hovered between 4 and 6 billion. Almost all of it occurred in the final half hour.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  SEEN\par \par \uc2 Though traders can never definitively confirm the presence of the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  in the market, Friday's late-day action appeared to be a clear case, as there was little other reason for a sudden upsurge of dollar demand.\par \par \uc2 "I'm 80 percent certain that this was \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a trader at a joint-stock bank in Shanghai.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  typically conducts its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  via transactions with large state-owned banks that are invisible to other market participants. The \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's counterparties then pass that liquidity through to the rest of the market.\par \par \uc2 Traders said that Friday's apparent action by the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  does not necessarily signal a shift in policy, but rather may have been a gesture to temporarily ease pressure on banks at month-end.\par \par \uc2 Banks report their net open \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of each month, and they prefer not to report large positions either long or short.\par \par \uc2 Friday's action may have been an effort to allow banks to unload long dollar positions that they have been saddled with for weeks.\par \par \uc2 A similar late-day surge of dollar buying occurred last Friday.\par \par \uc2 But traders say the daily pattern of the yuan hitting its top-end limit could resume next week.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHINA-YUAN-CLOSE/ | ABN | D | E | RBN | C | GRO | M | 