\par\par \b \uc2 CNH Tracker-China hastening reforms as offshore yuan languishes\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michelle Chen   \par \uc2 1,017 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2012\par 08:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Nov 29 (Reuters) - China is stepping up efforts to further liberalize its capital account by introducing a slew of measures to facilitate two-way cross-border fund flows, amid concerns that progress in internationalising the yuan may have stalled.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said more proactive policies to promote wider use of the yuan are likely to follow next year, especially in the form of encouraging yuan outflows, given that a once-a-decade handover of power in China is almost completed.\par \par \uc2 The grand plan of making the "redback" fully convertible in the forseeable future seems to have hit a roadblock recently, as offshore yuan liquidity keeps shrinking.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, global payments in yuan have fallen for two months in a row, as observed by SWIFT, a global transaction services organisation.\par \par \uc2 Yuan usage declined again in October, making it the 16th most used \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  payments table, two positions lower than the previous month, SWIFT said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Yuan payments decreased 10 percent while other countries increased by 9.3 percent compared to September, it added.\par \par \uc2 In a bid to inject more life into the market, authorities have taken several steps in the last few weeks.\par \par \uc2 Beijing plans a nearly three-fold jump in the quota for the Renminbi Qualified Foreign Investor (RQFII) scheme, which permits qualified investors to channel offshore yuan funds into mainland stock and bond markets. The quota will be raised by 200 billion yuan ($32.1 billion), regulators said in mid-November.\par \par \uc2 What's more, it also approved two cases of cross-border lending in yuan between companies within a week, which market players said marks a milestone in the yuan globalization process and opens a new channel for the accumulation of yuan offshore.\par \par \uc2 "The opening up of the capital account will be the main direction to further internationalise the yuan in future, since trade-related fund flows no longer have any restrictions," said Ngan Kim Man, head of the RMB business strategy and planning department at Hang Seng Bank.\par \par \uc2 Standard Chartered Bank (China) said on Monday it had secured approval for a 3.3 billion yuan loan quota on behalf of an American multi-national company, following the 150 million yuan quota that \uc2 China Construction Bank\uc2 's Shanghai branch secured for \uc2 General Electric\uc2  (China).\par \par \uc2 "You can see the significant increase of quota in Standard Chartered's case, which shows the regulators are feeling comfortable to let the yuan flow out through this channel," said Ngan.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect more yuan outflows under the capital account to be encouraged via cross-border lending and other schemes in the future, noting that policies this year which mainly focused on yuan repatriation caused some tightening in offshore liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's yuan deposits dropped for the second straight month in September to 545.7 billion yuan, 13 percent lower than the peak seen last November. The \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release October deposits data on Friday.\par \par \uc2 In addtition to the RQFII quota, some insurance companies were given approvals this year to enter the onshore interbank bond market to pursue higher returns with the offshore yuan they hold.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese government remains steadfast in supporting the development of the offshore yuan market, as evidenced by the latest key policy statements from the freshly completed 18th Communist Party Congress, said Bank of China International in a recent report.\par \par \uc2 WEEK IN REVIEW:\par \par \uc2 * Chinese asset management firm E Fund said on Tuesday it is considering applying for an additional quota under the Renminbi Qualified Foreign Institutional Investor (RQFII) programme, amid increasing demand for yuan-related products due to improved sentiment toward China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the economy.\par \par \uc2 * Chinese asset management firm CSOP's FTSE China A50 ETF\par \par \uc2 has been approved by the Hong Kong Stock Exchange as an eligible single Hong Kong stock for derivative warrant issuance. Warrants tracking its HK counter could be available for trading in the first week of December.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 China Construction Bank\uc2  , the country's No.2 lender by market value, finishes its sale of a 1 billion yuan, three-year dim sum bond in London at a coupon of 3.2 percent. All funds raised will be used to develop the bank's offshore yuan business and for other general corporate purposes.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Datang International\uc2  (Hong Kong), a wholly-owned subsidiary of \uc2 Datang International Power Generation\uc2 , sells a 500 million yuan three-year dim sum bond at 5.2 percent, according to IFR, a Thomson Reuters publication. Agricultural Bank of China Hong Kong branch, \uc2 Industrial and Commercial Bank of China\uc2  (Asia) and \uc2 Wing Lung Bank\uc2  are joint lead managers and bookrunners.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  said on Tuesday China did not meet the legal requirements to be deemed a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator, though its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained "significantly undervalued". It also said \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had "substantially" reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since the third quarter of 2011 and loosened capital controls.\par \par \uc2 CHART OF THE WEEK:\par \par \uc2 RMB lost two positions in October as world payments \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/zys34t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/zys34t}}}\par \par \uc2 LEAGUE TABLES\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Book runner:        Proceeds (RMB mln):       # of issues:  \par  1. \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2                 39,622.2                    121     \par  2. Standard            18,631.5                     72     \par     Chartered Bank     \par  3. \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas SA\f28 \uc2 \f2       15,511.3                     56     \par  4. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2        10,321.3                     15    \par  5. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2         6,988.5                     27      \par  \par  \par  YTD synthetic RMB bond issuance:       \par  Book runner:         Proceeds (RMB mln):       # of issues: \par  \par  1. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2        4,479.2                       3    \par  2. Citi                2,912.5                       2    \par  3. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2        2,312.5                       1    \par  4. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2      2,312.5                       1     \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2     \par  5. \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2                 1,248.5                       2     \par  \par  * Thomson Reuters data as of Nov. 29. \par     \par   RECENT STORIES:\par CNH Tracker-Yuan strength, capital inflows underpin dim sum\par treasuries \par  \par More stories about the CNH market                 \par Daily onshore yuan reports                        \par Daily China money market reports                  \par    \par Offshore yuan rate    Onshore yuan rate  \par Offshore yuan dealt Onshore yuan on CFETS \par Offshore yuan bonds \par  \par THOMSON REUTERS SPEED GUIDES  \par