\par\par \b \uc2 ICBC-Yuan set to be more flexible\b0\par\par\uc2 794 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2012\par \uc2 ENP Newswire\par \uc2 ENPNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012, Electronic News Publishing. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 Release date - 30102012\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We expect such fluctuation limits to be extended from the current 1 percent to 2.5 percent after the United States presidential election, and the 18th National Congress of the Communist Party of China (due to start on Nov 8),\u8217\'20\'19 said Lu Zhengwei, chief economist at the Industrial Bank.\par \par \uc2 He said interest rates and banks\u8217\'20\'19 reserve requirement ratio are unlikely to be adjusted in November given the current economic situation.\par \par \uc2 Li Wei\uc2 , an economist at Standard Chartered Bank, said: \u8216\'20\'18No one can rule out the possibility that the trading band is further widened. Such a move would send a strong signal to the market that the yuan is further liberalized and more market-driven.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This would also be in line with China\u8217\'20\'19s long-term economic reform in a bid to improve market efficiency.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 He declined to comment on the possible timing for such a move, but said a more flexible yuan will eventually come about and Chinese businesses will have to adapt to this change and come up with better business practices.\par \par \uc2 Chen Daofu, policy research chief of the Financial Research Institute at the State Council\u8217\'20\'19s Development Research Center, said: \u8216\'20\'18The current fluctuation limits already seem sufficient for the market.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 He said broadening the yuan\u8217\'20\'19s range depends on the demand of market players, and if market forces demonstrate greater appetite for trading in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such a decision might follow.\par \par \uc2 The People\u8217\'20\'19s Bank of China\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , announced in April that the yuan would be allowed to fluctuate by 1 percent from a daily mid-point - double the previous 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has depreciated against the dollar while the world\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest economy slowed for seven consecutive quarters, before starting to pick up in recent months as it stabilizes and major economies such the US, the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , the United Kingdom and Japan announced new easing policies.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has strengthened more than 2.4 percent since touching its weakest point of the year at 6.3967 in late July. Compared with the start of the year, it has appreciated by 0.8 percent.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18What the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to fix now is not to broaden the floating band of the yuan, but to solve the deviation in the daily reference rate it set from the real market situation,\u8217\'20\'19 said Ding Zhijie, dean of the School of Banking and Finance at the University of International Business and Economics in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18If we look at the past few months since the band was broadened to 1 percent, 99 percent of the daily yuan fluctuations did not touch the upper and lower limits at all.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 He said the problem is that the official daily pricing cannot sufficiently reflect market demand. \u8216\'20\'18For instance, today (Monday), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the mid-point at 6.299 against the dollar. In just 15 minutes the trading price went to 6.245.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the mid-point for the yuan had been increasing for three straight days, hitting its strongest level since May 11.\par \par \uc2 Yu Yongding, a former adviser to \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said in September that it is time for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and let the yuan float freely.\par \par \uc2 Liu Yuhui, director of the financial lab at the \uc2 Chinese Academy of Social Sciences\uc2 , said China should take advantage of the opportunity that market sentiment might drive down the dollar to broaden the floating range of the yuan.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It is easier for policymakers now to allow market pressures to operate in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market than it was before, as conditions have changed,\u8217\'20\'19 said Louis Kuijs, chief China economist at the \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland Group\uc2  and a former \uc2 World Bank\uc2  economist.\par \par \uc2 Previously, with a large balance of payments surplus, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  massively to prevent market pressures from driving the yuan up sharply. \u8216\'20\'18As such a surplus came down ... it can at the moment let the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  be determined largely by market forces without seeing a sharp appreciation,\u8217\'20\'19 Kuijs said.\par \par \uc2 Widening the band could make sense as a controlled next step in financial and monetary reform, he said, adding that China\u8217\'20\'19s economy and financial system are robust enough to withstand further flexibility in the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18In any case, it would be more appropriate than moving aggressively on opening the capital account while keeping the exchange rate regime as it is.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A more flexible exchange rate regime is needed to move to a more interest rate-oriented monetary policy and is also a condition for further opening up the capital account, Kuijs said.\par \par \uc2 [Editorial queries for this story should be sent to newswire@enpublishing.co.uk]\par \par \uc2 Dokument ENPNEW0020121031e8av0009a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
