\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan extends rise on euro strength\b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2012\par 11:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yuan hits strong side limit in afternoon trading\par \par \uc2 * Demand spurred by euro strength against dollar\par \par \uc2 * C.bank reverses three straight days of stronger fixes\par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Oct 30 (Reuters) - China's yuan briefly touched on the strong side trading limit in Monday's afternoon session, as traders pointed towards a euro rally against the dollar as propping up demand.\par \par \uc2 The yuan opened at 6.2430 per dollar, but weakened in morning trading when it looked unlikely to trouble the strong side limit.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened in the afternoon session, briefly hitting the edge of the strong side trading band before weakening slightly to close at 6.2405 against Monday's 6.2436.\par \par \uc2 The yuan/dollar exchange rate can rise or fall 1 percent from the mid-point set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  each day.\par \par \uc2 A sharp strengthening of the euro against the dollar that began around 2pm (0600 GMT) supported the yuan's appreciation in the afternoon session, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The yuan tends to track the performance of the euro and other global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  climbed 0.3 percent against the dollar to $1.2935, helped by lower Spanish and Italian bond yields.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  set its midpoint at 6.3028 per dollar, weaker than Monday's fix of 6.2992. That broke a sequence of three consecutive days when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened the yuan's midpoint, suggesting the bank had felt confident yuan demand has eased.\par \par \uc2 Despite touching the strong side boundary -- the third time since the limit was first reached last Thursday -- the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't hit Monday's record strong point of 6.2371.\par \par \uc2 Some traders said that demand had loosened as the rate reached a natural balance after its appreciation run since a year-low in late July.\par \par \uc2 However, others felt that the yuan could keep on strengthening without further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Shanghai newsroom; Editing by Jeremy Laurence)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 CHINA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -YUAN-CLOSE/ | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | ABX | BNX | FUN | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121102e8au000y9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
