\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  GLOBAL CALL: Our Take on the Day's Big  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  News\b0\par\par\uc2 1,005 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2012\par 13:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Energy Service\par \uc2 NRG\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Global Call covers the main talking points from a news meeting involving DJ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trader editors in New York, London and Singapore, as well as other \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  hot spots when warranted.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michael Casey\f28 \par \par \uc2 1. So much for the dollar/yen rally. For all the excitement over what looked like a major shift lower in the yen this week, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rebounded in the past 24 hours as traders calibrate their expectations for next week's meeting of the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 . In London trading the dollar was back below Y80. Meanwhile, options markets are already pricing for the likelihood that dollar/yen won't rise much further, which could be predicated on the belief that the BOJ won't live up to expectations for a heavy bout of quantitative easing. One concern is that although the market had begun to price in the prospect of an asset-buying program as large as Y20 trillion, constant jawboning from government officials on the need to reverse deflation and weaken the yen could give the BOJ cold feet as it seeks to protect its independence. In a BOJ Watch Friday, we reported that people familiar with the BOJ's thinking say an asset-buying program will be discussed at Tuesday's meeting, but they are already concerned about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's substantial, distorting impact on various asset classes.\par \par \uc2 2. In China, the yuan again hit the upper end of its trading band versus the dollar, as inflows into the country continued amid a general improvement in sentiment about its economic prospects. But a wave of dollar-buying by state banks left the impression that the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  was using them to conduct de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the yuan lower toward the end of the day.\par \par \uc2 3. In Berlin, a senior lawmaker from Germany's ruling coalition hinted that the Bundestag might be amenable to an extension in Greece's bailout program. Hans Michelbach, the senior finance policy spokesman for the Christian Social Union, the Bavarian sister party in German Chancellor Angela Merkel's conservative parliamentary alliance, told us exclusively that the German government was actively seeking to extend the Greece aid program. He said that was a "conceivable path." Support from the German parliament is critical if Greece is to turn an expected agreement with the EU-ECB-IMF "troika" for an extension to 2016 of its fiscal targets into a legally binding agreement and to secure an estimated EUR30 billion in funding needed to pay for the financial shortfall that this would entail.\par \par \uc2 4. Spain's unemployment numbers were, in Katie Martin's words, "hideous"--rising to 25.02% from 24.62%. But the market has become more or less inured to the depressing drumbeat of bad news out of Spain's economy. Nothing really changes the fact that Spanish Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy is going to have to ask for money from the EU sooner rather than later. And that, of course, would be welcomed by the market as it would trigger ECB bond-buying.\par \par \uc2 5. Portugal is also maneuvering slowly toward the prospect ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its bond market. It sold EUR50 million in 2018 notes in a private placement. That could help it attract ECB help because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it would only initiate its outright monetary transactions for countries that have proven access to funds from the market.\par \par \uc2 6. In his inaugural speech as the new governor of the Reserve Bank of New Zealand, \uc2 Graeme Wheeler\uc2  initially sparked a bit of excitement by mentioning the prospect of a rate cut and keeping the door open to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which helped push the New Zealand dollar lower early in Wellington trading. But in time, it became clear that there was no real shift in policy and that his positions on these policy options were consistent with those of his predecessors. The "kiwi" recovered and stabilized.\par \par \uc2 7. Across the Tasman Sea, however, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  has been surreptitiously engaging in a form of de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , writes James Glynn in an exclusive piece of analysis. The RBA, it turns out, has been allowing natural inflows of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into its coffers to drive its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves higher--by $890 million over the past two months. Normally, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would "sterilize" those inflows by purchasing local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its balance sheet steady, but it hasn't done so of late. It's an important reason that the Aussie dollar is under pressure.\par \par \uc2 8. In the latest expansion of the Libor scandal, we reported exclusively late in New York Thursday that nine additional banks have received subpoenas from the New York and Connecticut attorneys general as part of the international investigation into interest rate manipulation. The banks are \uc2 Bank of America Corp\uc2 ., \uc2 Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ, \uc2 Credit Suisse Group\uc2 , Lloyds, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2 , \uc2 Royal Bank of Canada\uc2 , \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 , \uc2 Norinchukin Bank\uc2  and West LB, according to the person familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 9. And in Singapore's own version of this global investigation--in this case a probe of how the Singapore Interbank Offered Rate (Sibor) is set--the \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland\uc2  has placed a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader, Ken Cho on leave, people familiar with the decision tell us. Choy is director of Emerging Markets \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the bank.\par \par \uc2 10. The central banks of Colombia and Mexico meet Friday. Both are expected to keep rates on hold.\par \par \uc2 11. In the U.S., the Commerce Department will release the first estimate of third quarter GDP at 8:30 a.m. EDT. It is expected to show an annualized gain of 1.8%, up from 1.5% in the previous quarter.\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 Michael Casey\uc2  is managing editor for the Americas at DJ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trader, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  news service jointly produced by Dow Jones Newswires and The Wall Street Journal.)\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2  [ 10-26-12 0751ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument NRG0000020121026e8aq0000w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
