\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-EMERGING MARKETS-Chile peso up on  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  data, Brazil real flat\b0\par\par\uc2 832 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2012\par 23:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso, Brazil real little changed\par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers; Adds details on Mexican peso)\par \par \uc2 By Natalia Cacioli and Moises Avila\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/SANTIAGO, Oct 25 (Reuters) - Chile's peso gained on Thursday on hopes Chinese factory output will accelerate at the end of the year and boost demand for South America's exports, but an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped gains in the real.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso gave up slight gains to weaken in late trading after weak quarterly earnings from \uc2 Apple Inc\uc2 , the most valuable public company in the United States, hit U.S. stock futures and investor appetite for riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso firmed 0.31 percent after a top Chinese official said the country's industrial output growth may be faster in the final three months of 2012 than in the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 China is the main consumer of Latin America's commodities exports and the positive outlook for the its economy boosted investors' appetite for risk in general.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso led gains among Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rising half a percentage point to 478.40 per dollar as the comments by the Chinese official boosted prices of copper, Chile's main export product.\par \par \uc2 "With copper and the euro rising, and stocks in positive territory, the (Chilean) peso could strengthen toward 478 units (per dollar)," said Jose Manuel Briceno, an analyst with GKFX in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso has appreciated around 8.5 percent so far this year, giving it a ranking as one of the top three performers among the 152 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Chile Finance Minister Felipe Larrain said late on Wednesday in New York that the government is seeking ways to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  without resorting to capital controls.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso slipped 0.15 percent to 13.01 per dollar and was set to close at its weakest in more than six weeks.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the most freely traded in Latin America, usually tracks other liquid risky assets such as U.S. stocks and the euro. The peso weakened in tandem with a drop in U.S. stock futures once Apple reported its results after the U.S. stock market close.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso has been one of the top-performing emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. But gains have flagged in recent weeks as investors cashed in on the rally.\par \par \uc2 Alfredo Puig, a trader at brokerage Vector in Monterrey, said the cost of dollars in pesos could weaken past its 200-day simple moving average to 13.20 per dollar if global market jitters persist.\par \par \uc2 The number of futures contracts betting on a stronger peso on the Chicago exchange hit a record high in late September. That position has fallen a bit, but the peso is still vulnerable to a stampede of investors who may try to get out of bullish bets at the same time.\par \par \uc2 "People think that the dollar shorts in Chicago are going to cover themselves due to the risk aversion we are seeing," Puig said.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, a much stronger government hand has been curbing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains and keeping the real at a tight trading range of 2.02-2.05 per dollar for the past several sessions.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reinforced the floor for the real early o n T hursday by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the second time this week.\par \par \uc2 The real traded nearly unchanged at 2.0240 per dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold nearly all the 30,000 reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps it offered in an auction, completing the early rollover of swaps that expire on Nov. 1.\par \par \uc2 Reverse swaps, or derivative contracts that emulate the purchase of dollars in the futures market, became the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's favorite instrument to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Combined with threats of additional government measures to curb inflows of speculative capital, those \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have drastically reduced liquidity and volatility in Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "The market is completely stuck. The government has already admitted we have a dirty-floating regime with strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jankiel Santos, chief economist at BES Investimento in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "The economic fundamentals point to a stronger real, but this is a market with very low liquidity due to government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2130 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          daily %  year-to\par                                   change   date %\par          