\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chile up on  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  data, Brazil may  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 726 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2012\par 01:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chinese manufacturing survey points to economic recovery\par \par \uc2 * Data shows Germany being sucked into euro zone crisis\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's Mantega admits "dirty float" of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso drops 0.12 pct, Chile peso up 0.35 pct\par \par \uc2 (Adds detail)\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte and Lorena Segura\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Oct 24 (Reuters) - Chile's peso bounced back from a two-month low o n Wednesday after data pointed to a stronger economic performance in China, the region's top trading partner, and a top buyer of Chilean copper.\par \par \uc2 After slipping for four straight sessions to trade at its weakest since August, C hile's peso strengthene d 0 .3 5 p ercent a fter data showed Chinese manufacturers' output reached a three-month high in October, while order books were at their highest level since April.\par \par \uc2 "The peso is supported by China's strong manufacturing data, which boosted copper prices and European stocks," said Jose Manuel Briceno, an analyst with GKFX in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 Copper, Chile's main export product, traded slightly higher on the London Metal Exchange.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso dipped 0. 1 2 percent, however, as investors remained worried about the global economy after business surveys suggested Germany is being sucked into the euro zone crisis.\par \par \uc2 The peso slumped to a nearly six-week intraday low on Wednesday, breaking past 13 per dollar before bouncing back to trade at 12.99.\par \par \uc2 Data on Wednesday showed Mexican annual inflation eased in the first half of October from a 2-1/2 year high, bolstering expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep borrowing costs steady into 2014. [nL 3E8LO5LY].\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve said it would stick to its stimulus plan until the job market improves, in line with expectations.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's asset buying scheme is expected to help support demand for higher-yielding, riskier assets in coming months. A nalysts said that demand for Mexican assets could keep the peso from breaking past 13 per dollar. [ID :nL1E8LNFFD]\par \par \uc2 "We still have the idea that the exchange rate can return to levels around 12.80 plus or minus 10 centavos, " said Rafael Camarena, a n economist at Santander.\par \par \uc2 DIRTY FLOAT\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, the real edged up 0.1 percent to 2.0250 per greenback.\par \par \uc2 T raders were unwilling to push it much stronger amid e xpecta tions that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening.\par \par \uc2 The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday after a two-week hiatus with an auction of reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps - derivative contracts that emulate the purchase of dollars in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 With the sale, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rolled over about half of the contracts that expire on Nov. 1, leaving traders speculating that it could offer more swaps in the next few days to complete the rollover, or even increase the stock of reverse swaps if dollar inflows pick up.\par \par \uc2 In the latest sign of the government commitment to a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2  acknowledged in an interview that the real is now subject to a "dirty-floating" regime in which policymakers \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep an exchange rate favorable to the local industry.\par \par \uc2 The constant threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sapped volumes and liquidity of the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, keeping the real in an increasingly tight trading range.\par \par \uc2 "We still work with a trading band of 2.0-2.1 reais per dollar, but the truth is that this range has been tightening. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever the real nears the level of 2.02 per dollar," said Mauricio Nakahodo, an economic research consultant with Tokyo-Mitsubishi bank in Sao Paulo.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      daily  year-t\par                                  %   -date\par                     Latest  change       %\par                                     change\par Brazil real           2.0245    0.10   -7.71\par                                     \par Mexico peso          12.9900    0.00    7.54\par                                     \par Argentina peso*       6.3500   -0.47  -25.51\par                                     \par Chile peso          481.0000    0.35    7.96\par                                     \par Colombia peso      1,816.850   -0.04    6.69\par                                     \par Peru sol              2.5830   -0.04    4.41\par                                     \par * Argentine peso's rate                     \par between brokerages                    \par                                           \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Moises Avila in Santiago, Natalia Cacioli in Sao Paulo, and Lorena Segura in Mexico; Editing by Phil Berlowitz and Diane Craft)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | R