\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  pick-up fails to spur Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen\b0\par\par\uc2 1,028 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2012\par 03:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Singapore dlr dips as c.bank spotted buying U.S. dlr\par \par \uc2  * Some suspect Seoul \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; won at 6-mth high vs yen\par \par \uc2  * Philippine peso down on dlr-short covering \par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2  By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Oct 18 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased on Thursday, even though Chinese data supported a year-end rebound in the world's No.2 economy, as regional central banks were spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the strength of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Many emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  started the day firmer after solid U.S. housing data and growing hopes that Spain will ask for a bailout next month boosted optimism on the global economy.\par \par \uc2  However, they turned slightly weaker or gave up most of their initial gains as the Singapore dollar fell, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore\uc2  (MAS) seen buying the U.S. dollar to slow down gains in this year's best performing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Some dealers in Seoul also suspected South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities of selling the won, which hit hit a near six-month high versus the yen. Major South Korean companies compete with Japanese firms in key overseas markets.\par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso eased as investors took profit amid caution that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to allow the local unit strengthen past 41.20 per dollar.\par \par \uc2  "Asian countries may have no choice but to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets or cut rates as recent economic data have been pretty bad, although a rebound in China's economy may help," said Yuna Park, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond analyst at \uc2 Dongbu Securities\uc2  in Seoul.\par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly slashed its main interest rate to shore up domestic demand as the economy might be weaker than forecast in 2013 due to a gloomy global outlook. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by regional authorities came even as \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy showed signs of improvement, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  The world's second-largest market slowed for a seventh straight quarter in July-September, but industrial production, retail sales and investment data were all slightly better than expected. \par \par \uc2  Those indicators eased worries about sluggish China growth, suggesting emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were eventually likely to rise further, dealers and analysts said.\par \par \uc2  The economic concerns, along with the euro zone's debt crisis, have been one of major hurdles to appreciation in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "China data could be signaling a bottoming out for China and the risk rally is still in play," said a European bank dealer in Manila.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar edged lower as the MAS was spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar's nominal effective exchange rate (NEER) earlier in the day was around 1.4 percent above its perceived parity with the extreme strong end of the NEER currently estimated at around 1.2170 per U.S. dollar, \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2  RINGGIT\par \par \uc2  The ringgit advanced, but it gave up most of the initial rise as a weaker Singapore dollar caused investors to cover dollar-short positions.\par \par \uc2  Dollar demand linked to daily fixing also put pressure on the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  But the ringgit is still holding upside momentum as worries about a global slowdown ease.\par \par \uc2  "Investors bought back dollars, but only to sell around 3.05 again. I will sell dollars or keep short positions as long as the euro stays above 1.3," said a Malaysian bank dealer in Kuala Lumpur.\par \par \uc2  The euro stood at $1.3104.\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  The won edged up against the dollar, but its upside was capped as caution over dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities prompted investors to take profits.\par \par \uc2  Some traders suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut gains, even though Chinese data eased worries about a slowdown in South Korea's top overseas market.\par \par \uc2  "Dollar bids elevated even after the good Chinese data," said a foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2  The won strengthened 0.4 percent to 13.9344 against the yen, its strongest since April 27.\par \par \uc2  Major South Korean companies such as \uc2 Hyundai Motor Co\par \par \uc2 compete with Japanese peers including \uc2 Toyota Motor Corp\uc2  in export markets.\par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso slid as investors covered dollar-short positions, with traders wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  also said the Philippines, along with Indonesia, has some weakness to address before it is likely to break into the investment-grade rating category. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers looked to buy the peso on dips, given the country's stronger economic fundamentals.\par \par \uc2  "Still, there is pretty much the chance for the upgrade, although I don't think people were expecting the upgrade to come this year," said a foreign bank dealer in Manila.\par \par \uc2  The dealer said he would buy the peso when it approaches near 41.40 per dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \par \par \uc2  Change on the day at 0650 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        79.12          78.92       -0.25\par  Sing dlr        1.2171         1.2162       -0.07\par  Taiwan dlr      29.202         29.246       +0.15\par  Korean won     1104.01        1105.50       +0.13\par  Baht             30.62          30.62       +0.00\par  Peso             41.27          41.19       -0.21\par  Rupiah         9590.00        9570.00       -0.21\par  Rupee            52.94          52.87       -0.12\par  Ringgit         3.0330         3.0360       +0.10\par  Yuan            6.2555         6.2545       -0.02\par  Change so far in 2012\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        79.12          76.92       -2.78\par  Sing dlr        1.2171         1.2969       +6.56\par  Taiwan dlr      29.202         30.290       +3.73\par  Korean won     1104.01        1151.80       +4.33\par  Baht             30.62          31.55       +3.04\par  Peso             41.27          43.84       +6.23\par  Rupiah         9590.00        9060.00       -5.53\par  Rupee            52.94          53.08       +0.27\par  Ringgit         3.0330         3.1685       +4.47\par  Yuan     