\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Recent economic comments from China's top officials\b0\par\par\uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2012\par 11:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BEIJING, Sept 21 (Reuters) - China's leaders have pledged to step up policy action in the second-half of 2012 to bolster an economy that has slowed for six successive quarters and is on course for its slackest year of expansion since 1999.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut interest rates twice in June and July and China's most powerful economic planner, the \uc2 National Development and Reform Commission\uc2 , said earlier in September it had fast-tracked $157 billion worth of infrastructure investments since May.\par \par \uc2 Below are recent comments on the economy from members of the top government leadership and senior institutional chiefs.\par \par \uc2 XI JINPING, VICE PRESIDENT\par \par \uc2 "We have full confidence in our ability to speed up the shift of growth model, stabilise external demand, expand domestic demand and build a society of higher level initial prosperity in an all-round way that benefits the over one billion people."\par \par \uc2 Source: \uc2 Xinhua\uc2  report, Sept 21\par \par \uc2 WEN JIABAO, PREMIER\par \par \uc2 "In recent months, China has been continuing to invest in euro zone government bonds and bonds issued by the European Financial Stability Facility (EFSF).\par \par \uc2 "Europe is one of the main markets for China to invest its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and China will continue to participate in efforts to tackle Europe's debt crisis through appropriate channels."\par \par \uc2 Source: Speech to business conference in Brussels, Sept 20\par \par \uc2 CHEN DEMING, MINISTER OF COMMERCE\par \par \uc2 "It is difficult for China's trade environment to improve significantly in the following months due to many unfavourable factors."\par \par \uc2 "Although it is very difficult to achieve the annual trade growth target, we should use all conceivable ways to fight for it."\par \par \uc2 SOURCE: Ministry of Commerce website, Sept 17\par \par \uc2 XIN CHANGXING, VICE MINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCES AND SOCIAL SECURITY\par \par \uc2 "Based on our surveys on 600 companies, they are keeping the level of employment stable. The total amount of workers employed is almost in line with last year. China has not seen any widespread layoffs.\par \par \uc2 "But the slowing economic growth is starting to affect the employment situation gradually, with the growth pace of newly created jobs moderating since April."\par \par \uc2 "Based on our survey of more than 100 job markets, demand for workers and the number of job hunters are both decelerating."\par \par \uc2 SOURCE: News conference, Sep 10\par \par \uc2 ZHONG SHAN, VICE COMMERCE MINISTER\par \par \uc2 "China's trade situation is very grim this year and it is very difficult to achieve the growth target set earlier this year."\par \par \uc2 SOURCE: International Business Daily, Aug 29\par \par \uc2 WANG CHAO, VICE COMMERCE MINISTER\par \par \uc2 "China and the United States should improve macro-economic policy coordination, work together to fight trade protectionism and avoid politicising trade issues.\par \par \uc2 "The two countries should also broaden the scope of trade and investment with each other.\par \par \uc2 "China has been focusing on boosting domestic consumption and transforming its economic growth model, which will create more investment opportunities for foreign countries, including the United States."\par \par \uc2 SOURCE: An academic forum in Beijing, Aug 28\par \par \uc2 YI GANG, HEAD OF CHINA'S STATE ADMINISTRATION OF \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 "The exchange rate of the renminbi is very close to equilibrium. With China's GDP per capita exceeding 5,000 yuan ($795), domestic companies will grow rapidly, which may continue for 20 years.\par \par \uc2 "China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stayed steady over the past year, showing that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees basically balanced cross-border \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par capital inflows and outflows."   \par  SOURCE: China Securities, July 23   \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting By China Economics Team; Editing by Nick Edwards)\f28 \par \par \uc2 CHINA-ECONOMY/OFFICIALS (FACTBOX) | ABN | C | GRO | MTL | SOF | D | E | RBN | G | M | O | OIL | Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120921e89l000o1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
